WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿1

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:14.394
Modern art.


00:00:14.395 --> 00:00:16.439
Yes, ladies and gentlemen.


00:00:16.898 --> 00:00:19.691
Until the National Socialists
came to power,


00:00:19.692 --> 00:00:24.947
Germany had such a thing as "modern" art,
which means...


00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:31.329
as one can conclude from the very name,
a different kind of art every year.


00:00:32.455 --> 00:00:36.124
What National Socialism wants
is a return to German art,


00:00:36.125 --> 00:00:40.837
which like all the creative values
of a people,


00:00:40.838 --> 00:00:42.382
must be based on timeless values.


00:00:43.841 --> 00:00:47.302
But if it no longer represents
these timeless values for our people,


00:00:47.303 --> 00:00:52.140
then it is without value even today.


00:00:52.141 --> 00:00:54.935
THE WORLD IS ONE BIG BROTHEL


00:00:54.936 --> 00:01:00.817
German women are mocked
and depicted as prostitutes.


00:01:01.818 --> 00:01:05.613
Soldiers are presented as murderers
or the victims of senseless slaughter


00:01:06.239 --> 00:01:09.950
in line with what they call
the "Bolshevik class struggle."


00:01:09.951 --> 00:01:15.622
Every attempt is made to eradicate
from our hearts the deep-rooted respect


00:01:15.623 --> 00:01:17.625
we naturally have for a soldier's courage.


00:01:18.584 --> 00:01:24.048
And madness, mental illness,
is elevated to a defining principle.


00:01:26.217 --> 00:01:31.973
Must one really assume that there are men
who actually see their compatriots


00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:34.182
only as degenerate cretins?


00:01:34.183 --> 00:01:37.894
People who see fields as blue,
the sky as green


00:01:37.895 --> 00:01:41.065
and clouds as sulfur yellow?


00:01:41.816 --> 00:01:45.278
They would, of course,
insist I not say "see," but "perceive."


00:01:46.195 --> 00:01:47.988
There are only two possibilities.


00:01:47.989 --> 00:01:51.242
Either these so-called "artists"


00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:53.577
really do see things that way


00:01:53.578 --> 00:01:56.122
and consequently
believe in what they depict.


00:01:56.664 --> 00:02:01.084
Here it would be important
to determine whether their flawed vision


00:02:01.085 --> 00:02:04.088
is the result of an accident
or of hereditary disease.


00:02:05.006 --> 00:02:09.259
In the former case, regrettable
for these unfortunate individuals.


00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:12.763
In the latter, information
for the Reich Ministry of the Interior,


00:02:12.764 --> 00:02:16.892
which could at least ensure
that such a gruesome ocular affliction


00:02:16.893 --> 00:02:21.355
is not passed on to future generations.


00:02:22.273 --> 00:02:23.356
The other possibility


00:02:23.357 --> 00:02:27.779
is that they themselves do not believe
in the reality of what they depict,


00:02:28.362 --> 00:02:30.573
but have other motives


00:02:31.115 --> 00:02:33.951
for pestering the nation
with this nonsense.


00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:38.956
In that case, such transgressions fall
within the realm of criminal activity.


00:02:40.625 --> 00:02:42.502
What does this have to do with art?


00:02:43.002 --> 00:02:47.255
How does it elevate the soul?
How does it show artistic ability?


00:02:47.256 --> 00:02:49.550
For to produce art, one must be an artist.


00:02:52.512 --> 00:02:54.555
I think you're artist enough
to do this too.


00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:01.729
Yes, you certainly could. Have a go.


00:03:02.271 --> 00:03:07.652
And when you've finished, ask your parents
if they'll give you ten cents for it.


00:03:09.737 --> 00:03:13.991
Would you like to know how much they paid
Mr. Vastly Kandinsky for this?


00:03:14.826 --> 00:03:16.285
2,000 marks.


00:03:16.619 --> 00:03:19.664
More than a year's wages
for a German worker.


00:03:20.456 --> 00:03:21.666
What does your dad do?


00:03:23.084 --> 00:03:25.002
He doesn't have a job right now.


00:03:27.463 --> 00:03:32.885
2,000 marks taken from taxes
paid by the working German population.


00:03:37.723 --> 00:03:41.060
We have seen to it here that the people...


00:03:48.568 --> 00:03:51.320
Maybe I don't want
to be a painter after all.


00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.617
Don't tell anybody, but I like it.


00:04:05.877 --> 00:04:07.879
"DEGENERATE ART" EXHIBITION


00:04:13.301 --> 00:04:16.929
Aunt Elisabeth,
did you see the way they looked at you?


00:04:17.847 --> 00:04:20.181
On Monday,
nobody here will have eyes for me.


00:04:20.182 --> 00:04:22.184
They'll all be cheering the fuhrer.


00:04:23.436 --> 00:04:25.980
- Good day.
- I think you're better than Hitler.


00:04:29.066 --> 00:04:31.109
- Good day.
- Good day, young lady.


00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:33.321
You took your nephew on an outing.


00:04:33.654 --> 00:04:35.031
- Yes.
- Thank you.


00:04:38.659 --> 00:04:40.912
- I wish you a pleasant ride.
- Thank you.


00:04:55.968 --> 00:04:58.763
Over there,
that's where our apartment was.


00:05:03.142 --> 00:05:05.311
What do you miss most about Dresden?


00:05:09.732 --> 00:05:11.734
Sometimes it helps to talk about it.


00:05:17.198 --> 00:05:19.115
I know who you miss most!


00:05:19.116 --> 00:05:21.452
That little girl with the red braids.


00:05:22.536 --> 00:05:25.122
What was her name again? Johanna?


00:05:25.623 --> 00:05:28.792
Johanna, right? Your beloved. Right?


00:05:28.793 --> 00:05:30.336
Not only Johanna.


00:05:30.836 --> 00:05:33.547
- Who else do you miss?
- The Schréders.


00:05:33.881 --> 00:05:37.218
You know, the old couple in our building.


00:05:37.885 --> 00:05:41.597
The ones that always hold hands
like little kids.


00:05:41.931 --> 00:05:42.932
I like them.


00:05:43.724 --> 00:05:45.308
And their dachshund, Thilo.


00:05:45.309 --> 00:05:48.604
He always comes to me
when I call his name.


00:05:53.192 --> 00:05:56.153
It's only 45 kilometers from us
to Dresden.


00:05:56.612 --> 00:05:58.906
You'll be able to visit them
as often as you like.


00:06:10.543 --> 00:06:13.713
But you're right.
Dresden is unbeatable in its beauty.


00:06:35.401 --> 00:06:36.485
You know what?


00:06:37.695 --> 00:06:40.656
I find your father very strong
for not joining the Nazi Party.


00:06:41.532 --> 00:06:43.283
One signature,


00:06:43.284 --> 00:06:46.203
he could have kept his teaching job
and the apartment.


00:06:47.455 --> 00:06:50.708
He says it's criminal, the way the Nazis...


00:06:51.042 --> 00:06:54.795
I know. You don't talk like this
to anyone else, do you?


00:06:55.546 --> 00:06:58.590
Mama says she'll get him to join anyways.


00:06:58.591 --> 00:07:01.510
After the war,
being a member will be his capitol.


00:07:02.261 --> 00:07:03.554
That's "capital"!


00:07:37.838 --> 00:07:39.714
- Good-bye, Miss May.
- Good-bye.


00:07:39.715 --> 00:07:41.008
Good-bye.


00:08:07.201 --> 00:08:08.410
Hold this for a moment.


00:08:08.994 --> 00:08:11.539
Did you forget something, Aunt Elisabeth?


00:08:21.549 --> 00:08:24.718
Hey, Eddie. The May girl is here again.


00:08:25.052 --> 00:08:26.719
Let's make her happy.


00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:28.222
- Kai?
- Ready.


00:08:28.764 --> 00:08:31.266
- Good.
- All at the same time.


00:08:31.267 --> 00:08:35.604
Good. On the count of three.
One... two... three.


00:09:39.001 --> 00:09:40.085
Take care.


00:09:42.504 --> 00:09:43.589
Thank you.


00:09:51.263 --> 00:09:53.515
To paint a picture
which makes you feel that way.


00:09:54.016 --> 00:09:57.144
That's what they're trying to do,
those "degenerate" artists.


00:10:04.568 --> 00:10:08.238
Elisabeth, you're late again.
You look a mess!


00:10:08.239 --> 00:10:10.407
Chest out! Chin up!


00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:22.086
You, in the first row. Come.


00:10:25.923 --> 00:10:27.341
You'll give him the bouquet.


00:10:46.235 --> 00:10:48.904
Heil! Heil! Heil!


00:12:27.086 --> 00:12:28.128
Don't look away.


00:12:30.422 --> 00:12:31.840
Never look away, Kurt.


00:12:33.884 --> 00:12:36.678
Everything that's true is beautiful.


00:13:01.995 --> 00:13:03.122
This note.


00:13:05.207 --> 00:13:07.251
It contains the whole power of music...


00:13:08.961 --> 00:13:10.378
of life itself,


00:13:10.379 --> 00:13:12.047
of the entire universe.


00:13:14.758 --> 00:13:17.428
People look for the code of the world.


00:13:18.178 --> 00:13:19.221
But here it is!


00:13:22.433 --> 00:13:23.559
Here.


00:13:25.853 --> 00:13:26.937
Do you hear that?


00:13:30.190 --> 00:13:33.777
The A above middle C
on the May's family piano in Großschönau.


00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:37.823
And now that I've found it...


00:13:40.284 --> 00:13:42.286
I can play it anywhere.


00:13:50.252 --> 00:13:51.253
On the table.


00:13:54.256 --> 00:13:55.507
Can you hear it?


00:13:57.342 --> 00:13:58.719
Even on my head.


00:14:00.804 --> 00:14:04.558
- Aunt Elisabeth, you're bleeding.
- Even on my head.


00:14:07.603 --> 00:14:08.770
Elisabeth!


00:14:09.938 --> 00:14:11.690
For God's sake, what are you doing?


00:14:12.524 --> 00:14:14.276
Playing a concert for the Führer!


00:14:18.655 --> 00:14:22.033
"Youthful delusion."
That almost sounds harmless.


00:14:22.034 --> 00:14:26.079
"Mild schizophrenia, youthful delusion."
I can hear you!


00:14:27.331 --> 00:14:30.751
But nothing that can't be healed
by some time away.


00:14:31.502 --> 00:14:33.461
Time away in...


00:14:33.462 --> 00:14:35.004
In an institution, yes.


00:14:35.005 --> 00:14:37.715
Couldn't we try
giving her some rest at home first?


00:14:37.716 --> 00:14:43.054
She worked so hard to graduate and went
straight into the secretarial course...


00:14:43.055 --> 00:14:44.389
Elisabeth?


00:14:46.391 --> 00:14:48.769
Perhaps it's simply overexertion.


00:14:53.649 --> 00:14:55.150
Is this your wife?


00:14:57.653 --> 00:15:01.572
You can't stand her, right?
I can tell by your posture.


00:15:01.573 --> 00:15:02.783
Elisabeth!


00:15:03.909 --> 00:15:06.619
Kindly wait outside
until we've finished talking.


00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:08.205
I won't tell you again.


00:15:20.509 --> 00:15:23.845
As schizophrenia is a hereditary
condition, I'm obliged to ask.


00:15:24.263 --> 00:15:27.349
Are there other cases of mental illness
in your family?


00:15:27.808 --> 00:15:29.518
For God's sake, no!


00:15:30.978 --> 00:15:34.022
- Depression?
- We're all cheerful people.


00:15:35.107 --> 00:15:38.110
We doctors are the guardians
of the flow of hereditary health.


00:15:38.485 --> 00:15:40.778
I must report this
to the Health Authority.


00:15:40.779 --> 00:15:43.865
The decision on the committal
may not be up to you.


00:15:47.578 --> 00:15:48.954
Dr. Michaelis...


00:15:51.081 --> 00:15:52.082
Franz.


00:15:52.541 --> 00:15:55.586
I knew your parents.
Even your grandparents.


00:15:56.336 --> 00:15:57.337
Please...


00:15:57.921 --> 00:15:59.131
Don't report it.


00:16:03.594 --> 00:16:05.095
As it's you, Mrs. May.


00:16:06.638 --> 00:16:09.141
But tell me right away
if her condition worsens.


00:16:11.143 --> 00:16:12.977
- Good-bye.
- Heil Hitler!


00:16:12.978 --> 00:16:16.148
- Of course. Heil Hitler.
- Heil Hitler.


00:16:39.379 --> 00:16:40.380
<i>Operator.</i>


00:16:40.881 --> 00:16:43.050
Connect me with the Health Authority.


00:16:45.969 --> 00:16:47.386
- Good-bye.
- Good-bye, Günther.


00:16:47.387 --> 00:16:49.348
Ms. May, we have to leave now.


00:16:50.223 --> 00:16:52.975
- Take care, sister.
- We'll miss you.


00:16:52.976 --> 00:16:54.728
It is only for a couple of weeks.


00:16:55.312 --> 00:16:56.605
We'll see each other soon.


00:16:58.106 --> 00:17:00.025
Good-bye, Ehrenfried.


00:17:01.401 --> 00:17:03.820
Good-bye. We'll miss you.


00:17:05.989 --> 00:17:07.407
I don't want to, Mama.


00:17:07.949 --> 00:17:09.493
Kurt, go back inside.


00:17:10.077 --> 00:17:11.078
Kurt!


00:17:12.079 --> 00:17:13.829
I don't want to go!


00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:15.040
Grab her legs.


00:17:19.086 --> 00:17:20.169
- Got her?
- Yes.


00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:21.505
No!


00:17:24.466 --> 00:17:26.593
- Come.
- Hold her still.


00:17:29.721 --> 00:17:31.765
She'll be quiet in a moment.


00:17:39.898 --> 00:17:41.692
Scopolamine. It works quickly.


00:17:46.363 --> 00:17:47.864
Let's strap her in.


00:17:57.791 --> 00:17:58.874
Her suitcase!


00:17:58.875 --> 00:18:00.210
Of course.


00:18:03.255 --> 00:18:05.757
- These are her things.
- Okay.


00:18:20.689 --> 00:18:22.232
Never look away!


00:18:48.133 --> 00:18:49.885
My dear colleagues,


00:18:50.761 --> 00:18:52.471
I'd like to congratulate you.


00:18:54.264 --> 00:18:56.432
Since we introduced the law,


00:18:56.433 --> 00:19:00.269
the weakest percentile of the German
population has been rendered infertile.


00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:01.897
400,000 individuals.


00:19:02.773 --> 00:19:04.191
A proud figure.


00:19:04.983 --> 00:19:06.901
A contribution towards positive breeding


00:19:06.902 --> 00:19:09.780
that future generations
will thank you for.


00:19:11.740 --> 00:19:14.450
It is now my hope
that we shall one day live


00:19:14.451 --> 00:19:18.496
in a world where the streets
are completely free


00:19:18.497 --> 00:19:23.126
of mongoloids, the mentally ill,
and other deformed individuals.


00:19:23.543 --> 00:19:27.964
But it is time to shift into higher gear.


00:19:29.049 --> 00:19:31.133
As a result of British air raids,


00:19:31.134 --> 00:19:33.970
we have an increased need
for auxiliary hospital places.


00:19:34.638 --> 00:19:38.766
We cannot permit a situation
whereby a wounded German soldier


00:19:38.767 --> 00:19:40.476
is denied a place in a hospital


00:19:40.477 --> 00:19:44.272
because it is being used
to take care of a useless life.


00:19:49.236 --> 00:19:52.322
How can we help you? What can we do?


00:19:53.281 --> 00:19:56.201
Thank you for asking that question, Carl.


00:19:58.995 --> 00:20:00.079
Gentlemen,


00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:03.917
from now on
you are not just doctors and SS officers.


00:20:04.209 --> 00:20:07.420
You are experts
at the Court of Hereditary Health.


00:20:07.629 --> 00:20:09.130
What does this mean?


00:20:09.673 --> 00:20:15.636
Well, any patient you have sterilized
and whose medical file you mark


00:20:15.637 --> 00:20:18.265
with a blue minus sign...


00:20:18.890 --> 00:20:20.475
remains in the institution.


00:20:21.101 --> 00:20:23.727
However,
if we find a red plus sign on the file,


00:20:23.728 --> 00:20:27.314
we know that the life in question
is a worthless one,


00:20:27.315 --> 00:20:31.443
and the patient will be transferred
to one of three special institutions


00:20:31.444 --> 00:20:34.698
in the eastern part of the Reich and there


00:20:35.073 --> 00:20:37.158
will be relieved
of a meaningless existence.


00:20:39.369 --> 00:20:40.537
Your pen.


00:20:41.872 --> 00:20:42.998
Your sword.


00:21:04.352 --> 00:21:07.563
Examination and preliminary interview.
Elisabeth May, 23 years old.


00:21:07.564 --> 00:21:10.566
Sterilization appointment today, 3:45 p.m.


00:21:10.567 --> 00:21:11.568
Thank you.


00:21:15.363 --> 00:21:17.908
You may enter.
The form of address is "Herr Professor."


00:21:44.643 --> 00:21:46.394
You may sit down there.


00:22:07.582 --> 00:22:09.000
Did your daughter paint that?


00:22:13.964 --> 00:22:15.674
Why do you think you are here?


00:22:19.219 --> 00:22:21.054
Because sometimes I don't think right.


00:22:22.180 --> 00:22:24.516
Do you know what kind of hospital
I am running here?


00:22:25.850 --> 00:22:27.018
A gynecological hospital.


00:22:30.522 --> 00:22:32.232
A very nice girl, your daughter.


00:22:34.651 --> 00:22:36.111
I can see from the picture.


00:22:37.362 --> 00:22:39.572
Not what you'd call artistically talented.


00:22:42.242 --> 00:22:43.962
I suppose
you might even be pleased by that?


00:22:45.078 --> 00:22:46.121
But a lot of heart.


00:22:48.748 --> 00:22:50.250
I have a nephew the same age.


00:22:50.959 --> 00:22:52.544
Unfortunately, he's very talented.


00:22:53.044 --> 00:22:55.839
I sometimes take him to exhibitions,
to encourage him.


00:22:58.591 --> 00:22:59.592
Good.


00:23:00.593 --> 00:23:03.555
Now please get on the examination chair
in the next room.


00:23:04.681 --> 00:23:05.890
You may keep...


00:23:06.391 --> 00:23:08.767
I insist on speaking to Professor Seeband!


00:23:08.768 --> 00:23:09.978
Excuse me for a moment.


00:23:11.730 --> 00:23:16.150
I've tried to get an appointment
for weeks and received no response.


00:23:16.151 --> 00:23:17.818
I'm entitled to speak with him!


00:23:17.819 --> 00:23:19.945
Excuse me, Professor. I couldn't stop him.


00:23:19.946 --> 00:23:21.197
Mr. Lohse-Wächtler.


00:23:22.490 --> 00:23:25.659
You asked me
if I wanted my daughter's suffering


00:23:25.660 --> 00:23:28.038
to be passed on to the next generation.


00:23:28.329 --> 00:23:30.164
That is why I agreed to the operation.


00:23:30.165 --> 00:23:33.167
But what about her suffering now?


00:23:33.168 --> 00:23:35.544
You're a German man. Compose yourself!


00:23:35.545 --> 00:23:36.962
And my suffering?


00:23:36.963 --> 00:23:39.257
I will not tolerate this tone any longer!


00:23:39.758 --> 00:23:42.010
I'll report you, Professor Seeband.


00:23:42.427 --> 00:23:44.054
To the Reich Medical Board.


00:23:45.680 --> 00:23:48.724
You do that, Mr. Lohse-Wächtler.
You do that.


00:23:48.725 --> 00:23:51.102
You're a doctor.
You've sworn the Hippocratic Oath.


00:23:51.394 --> 00:23:52.437
Let go of me!


00:23:52.937 --> 00:23:55.147
One day, this will all catch up with you!


00:23:55.148 --> 00:23:58.734
STERILIZATION APPOINTMENT 3:45 P.M.


00:23:58.735 --> 00:24:00.695
It will catch up with you!


00:24:01.321 --> 00:24:04.114
It will catch up with you for sure!


00:24:04.115 --> 00:24:06.784
It'll catch up with you,
Professor Seeband!


00:24:06.785 --> 00:24:08.369
One day!


00:24:20.715 --> 00:24:22.966
You should not have looked at that.


00:24:22.967 --> 00:24:25.719
My ancestry is sound. I know I'm healthy.


00:24:25.720 --> 00:24:27.429
Three experts disagree.


00:24:27.430 --> 00:24:29.015
- No!
- Sit down!


00:24:38.316 --> 00:24:41.196
You will first go to the examination room
and then to the operating room.


00:24:41.820 --> 00:24:43.947
And you will cooperate.


00:24:44.572 --> 00:24:47.866
Otherwise we will have to strap you down,
and it will be more difficult


00:24:47.867 --> 00:24:49.202
and more painful.


00:25:02.132 --> 00:25:05.009
Please. Mr. Seeband.


00:25:05.385 --> 00:25:08.096
Herr Professor, please.


00:25:09.097 --> 00:25:13.725
For the fuhrer... I'll bear many children.
Healthy, Aryan children.


00:25:13.726 --> 00:25:16.396
I'll give them to the Führer,
just as we are supposed to.


00:25:17.438 --> 00:25:21.192
And my children will give
their children to the Führer too.


00:25:21.818 --> 00:25:23.152
For the war!


00:25:23.153 --> 00:25:25.155
You need soldiers, don't you?


00:25:25.446 --> 00:25:27.115
You must need more soldiers!


00:25:27.740 --> 00:25:29.534
Who else will go to battle?


00:25:30.493 --> 00:25:33.413
I'm only confused sometimes.


00:25:33.997 --> 00:25:35.206
It's very seldom.


00:25:38.293 --> 00:25:40.003
I don't want to go!


00:25:43.798 --> 00:25:45.090
I need backup!


00:25:45.091 --> 00:25:46.801
You're a father too.


00:25:48.553 --> 00:25:50.929
Please, for your daughter. She paints too.


00:25:50.930 --> 00:25:53.975
- That's enough!
- I could be her sister.


00:25:54.350 --> 00:25:56.019
You could be my father.


00:25:56.895 --> 00:25:58.313
Please, Papa.


00:25:59.564 --> 00:26:00.607
Please, Papa!


00:26:01.399 --> 00:26:02.649
No!


00:26:02.650 --> 00:26:03.651
Papa!


00:26:04.944 --> 00:26:06.069
Papa!


00:26:06.070 --> 00:26:07.697
Please, Papa!


00:26:08.573 --> 00:26:10.283
Papa, please!


00:26:11.910 --> 00:26:13.328
Please, Papa!


00:26:30.094 --> 00:26:31.803
<i>- Anna.
- Yes, Herr Professor?</i>


00:26:31.804 --> 00:26:33.973
I will not perform the operation
on Miss May.


00:26:34.307 --> 00:26:35.474
Assign Blockmann.


00:26:35.475 --> 00:26:37.393
<i>But he's scheduled for the delivery room.</i>


00:26:37.810 --> 00:26:39.520
Then change the schedule!


00:27:36.619 --> 00:27:37.662
Thank you.


00:27:45.837 --> 00:27:49.215
You both look so handsome in your
uniforms. Elisabeth will be pleased.


00:27:52.760 --> 00:27:53.803
Johann.


00:27:54.971 --> 00:27:56.180
Yes.


00:27:59.267 --> 00:28:00.392
You know...


00:28:00.393 --> 00:28:02.812
I know.
After the war, it will be my capital.


00:28:03.313 --> 00:28:05.732
And don't forget the salute,
"Heil Hitler."


00:28:10.945 --> 00:28:15.073
If you can't bring yourself to say it,
just say <i>"drei liter"</i> quickly.


00:28:15.074 --> 00:28:16.326
Nobody will notice.


00:28:18.828 --> 00:28:20.996
And not a word
about your incessant painting.


00:28:20.997 --> 00:28:22.707
Especially the nudes!


00:28:36.179 --> 00:28:37.180
Heil Hitler!


00:28:37.597 --> 00:28:42.226
Drei <i>liter.</i> We have an appointment
to visit... Elisabeth May.


00:28:42.602 --> 00:28:44.896
I'm Johann Barnert, her brother-in-law.


00:28:45.438 --> 00:28:48.357
Her brothers, Ehrenfried and Günther May.


00:28:48.358 --> 00:28:50.067
Her sister, Waltraud.


00:28:50.068 --> 00:28:51.986
And her mother, Malvine.


00:28:53.488 --> 00:28:55.615
Please turn a little to the right.


00:28:56.074 --> 00:28:59.952
Miss Elisabeth May
was transferred the day before yesterday.


00:29:00.286 --> 00:29:02.412
Transferred? That's impossible.


00:29:02.413 --> 00:29:03.873
All look here, please.


00:29:04.290 --> 00:29:05.958
Orders from the Central Office.


00:29:08.336 --> 00:29:09.337
But where to?


00:29:10.421 --> 00:29:11.547
Aren't two missing?


00:29:12.173 --> 00:29:14.092
Käthe, we're waiting for you.


00:29:15.093 --> 00:29:16.552
Where has she been transferred?


00:29:18.471 --> 00:29:19.972
Großschweidnitz Hospital.


00:29:20.807 --> 00:29:22.058
Großschweidnitz?


00:29:22.558 --> 00:29:26.144
That's two days from here!
How are we supposed to visit her?


00:29:26.145 --> 00:29:29.482
We work,
and the boys are on leave from the front.


00:29:29.899 --> 00:29:31.609
I can't tell you any more than that.


00:29:32.151 --> 00:29:34.195
I have to go now. Heil Hitler!


00:29:35.863 --> 00:29:36.989
That's it.


00:29:47.083 --> 00:29:49.210
I'll write to the Health Ministry.


00:29:49.627 --> 00:29:51.212
Please look in this direction.


00:29:58.344 --> 00:30:00.346
FEBRUARY 13, 1945


00:30:48.186 --> 00:30:50.896
Tinfoil. I read about that.


00:30:50.897 --> 00:30:52.940
It's to interfere
with the radio and radar.


00:31:19.342 --> 00:31:22.220
Johanna! Johanna! Wake up!


00:31:26.098 --> 00:31:28.017
Mama! Mama!


00:31:41.239 --> 00:31:44.115
This way! There's a slope up there.


00:31:44.116 --> 00:31:45.576
Head down!


00:31:48.204 --> 00:31:49.330
<i>Günther!</i>


00:31:52.083 --> 00:31:53.167
Günther!


00:32:25.616 --> 00:32:28.285
I like you.


00:32:28.286 --> 00:32:30.037
I like you too.


00:33:52.703 --> 00:33:56.248
MAY 8, 1945


00:34:32.076 --> 00:34:33.202
Mr. Seeband?


00:34:33.953 --> 00:34:36.163
Professor Seeband. Yes, that's me.


00:35:09.363 --> 00:35:10.865
Mr. Seeband.


00:35:11.198 --> 00:35:12.324
Professor Seeband.


00:35:15.536 --> 00:35:16.537
What did he say?


00:35:17.663 --> 00:35:20.791
He wants to be addressed
as "Herr Professor."


00:35:31.093 --> 00:35:32.094
All right.


00:35:33.429 --> 00:35:35.097
Herr Professor.


00:35:42.772 --> 00:35:44.482
Where is Burghart Kroll?


00:35:45.232 --> 00:35:46.316
Who?


00:35:46.317 --> 00:35:47.485
Burghart Kroll.


00:35:51.822 --> 00:35:55.116
The head of the Reich Medical Work Group.


00:35:55.117 --> 00:35:57.453
We know about your meetings in Berlin.


00:35:58.829 --> 00:36:02.249
I have no idea what you're talking about.
I do not know this man.


00:36:15.471 --> 00:36:16.764
I still don't know him.


00:36:38.410 --> 00:36:42.414
If my child were born with health
problems, should it be put to death?


00:36:47.253 --> 00:36:51.298
It so happens that space
and resources on this earth are limited.


00:36:52.091 --> 00:36:55.094
Who should have them?
The healthy or the sick?


00:37:12.403 --> 00:37:15.531
Soon there will be
one more place available on this earth.


00:37:26.166 --> 00:37:28.752
You have not indicated
if you were a member of the Nazi Party.


00:37:29.753 --> 00:37:31.255
Were you a member of the Party?


00:37:31.630 --> 00:37:33.423
Principal, for many years...


00:37:33.424 --> 00:37:36.343
Yes or no, Mr. Barnert?


00:37:38.596 --> 00:37:39.722
Yes.


00:37:52.443 --> 00:37:53.861
But I'm not a Nazi.


00:37:54.445 --> 00:37:56.780
Three quarters of all teachers
were in the Party.


00:37:57.698 --> 00:38:02.077
And it is to the remaining quarter that we
shall entrust our children. Good day.


00:38:16.008 --> 00:38:17.551
Too hot!


00:38:26.560 --> 00:38:28.646
"The Patriotic War."


00:38:34.068 --> 00:38:36.946
"The Patriotic War...


00:38:39.365 --> 00:38:42.368
is... is special."


00:39:08.852 --> 00:39:09.853
Comrade!


00:39:12.815 --> 00:39:13.857
Comrade!


00:39:18.904 --> 00:39:20.113
What?


00:39:20.114 --> 00:39:22.782
The preliminary contractions are too long.


00:39:22.783 --> 00:39:24.863
The baby is in the wrong position.
It can't come out!


00:39:25.786 --> 00:39:26.787
What?


00:39:27.538 --> 00:39:30.082
Call the interpreter. Immediately.


00:39:49.852 --> 00:39:53.188
He is suspicious.
He asks why you want to help.


00:39:54.940 --> 00:39:56.316
I want to help because I can.


00:40:01.280 --> 00:40:02.322
You may go.


00:40:26.597 --> 00:40:30.392
A gypsy woman predicted
I'd never have children.


00:40:31.143 --> 00:40:32.770
It's my fate.


00:40:33.854 --> 00:40:37.608
- Place her sideways.
- Turn her sideways across the bed.


00:40:41.820 --> 00:40:42.863
Which week is she in?


00:40:44.907 --> 00:40:45.990
The 36th.


00:40:45.991 --> 00:40:47.117
Blood pressure?


00:40:48.660 --> 00:40:50.328
110 over 70.


00:40:50.329 --> 00:40:54.666
What a fool I am to believe
I could trick fate and have children!


00:40:56.752 --> 00:40:59.379
Tell her
she will definitely have one child.


00:40:59.797 --> 00:41:01.632
And if she wants, many more after that.


00:41:09.389 --> 00:41:11.266
The child is in the transverse position.


00:41:13.811 --> 00:41:16.480
During contractions,
the uterus is too hard to turn the child.


00:41:17.731 --> 00:41:20.191
I'll open the amniotic sac from inside.


00:41:20.192 --> 00:41:22.611
In a pause between contractions,
I'll turn the baby.


00:41:27.533 --> 00:41:29.118
I'm a military interpreter.


00:41:32.913 --> 00:41:33.997
Do it.


00:41:39.753 --> 00:41:41.046
Gloves, please.


00:41:49.054 --> 00:41:50.097
Vodka, please.


00:41:56.270 --> 00:41:58.105
Don't dry them. Don't touch.


00:42:04.319 --> 00:42:05.863
We'll do it without anesthesia.


00:42:17.374 --> 00:42:18.792
I already have a leg.


00:42:23.922 --> 00:42:26.383
We must wait for the next contraction.


00:42:28.635 --> 00:42:31.555
Now I'm placing the index finger
in the baby's mouth.


00:42:39.563 --> 00:42:41.773
Pressing the chin against the chest.


00:42:43.066 --> 00:42:45.485
And slowly pulling out the baby's head.


00:42:52.868 --> 00:42:55.495
A boy. A healthy boy.


00:43:13.513 --> 00:43:15.224
Alexander Mikhailovich!


00:43:19.394 --> 00:43:21.772
And a beautiful, healthy mother.


00:43:25.692 --> 00:43:27.527
Congratulations, Major.


00:43:41.458 --> 00:43:43.585
Whoever saves a life
saves the entire world.


00:43:45.921 --> 00:43:47.339
You have saved my world,


00:43:48.215 --> 00:43:49.341
Herr Professor.


00:43:51.468 --> 00:43:53.845
No one will harm a hair on your head.


00:43:54.680 --> 00:43:56.640
You are now under my personal protection.


00:43:59.518 --> 00:44:01.603
Prepare a guest room for the professor.


00:44:02.562 --> 00:44:04.314
And bring him some decent clothes.


00:44:16.076 --> 00:44:19.413
Look at him. This is our son.


00:46:01.306 --> 00:46:04.810
Father.
You don't have to worry any longer!


00:46:05.435 --> 00:46:08.605
Now I understand! I understand.


00:46:10.232 --> 00:46:11.565
What is it you understand?


00:46:11.566 --> 00:46:13.234
Everything.


00:46:13.235 --> 00:46:16.738
How everything is connected.
That everything is connected.


00:46:18.573 --> 00:46:19.950
The code of the world.


00:46:22.202 --> 00:46:23.245
<i>' 'L</i>


00:46:24.079 --> 00:46:27.958
I never have to worry again.
I never have to be afraid again.


00:46:28.542 --> 00:46:29.793
I'm untouchable.


00:46:32.421 --> 00:46:33.672
That's nice.


00:46:34.089 --> 00:46:35.756
No, Father, you don't understand.


00:46:35.757 --> 00:46:39.052
You don't have to worry either.
Really. And...


00:46:39.594 --> 00:46:42.930
I don't even have to be an artist.
I can choose any profession.


00:46:42.931 --> 00:46:46.810
And I will find what's right, what's true!


00:46:49.813 --> 00:46:51.690
I'm happy for you, really.


00:46:53.066 --> 00:46:54.626
I need to preserve this moment somehow!


00:46:55.277 --> 00:46:57.112
Somehow I need to preserve this moment.


00:47:02.993 --> 00:47:04.369
Now I understand.


00:47:14.421 --> 00:47:16.256
I know who it is you're thinking about.


00:47:17.007 --> 00:47:18.341
But he's different.


00:47:40.363 --> 00:47:43.283
STENCILING AND SIGNAGE STUDIOS
DRESDEN


00:47:52.918 --> 00:47:54.210
Good morning, Father.


00:47:54.211 --> 00:47:55.670
Good morning, my boy.


00:48:22.447 --> 00:48:24.074
Check the alignment, colleague.


00:48:51.351 --> 00:48:53.478
Do you do that
so you can feel better than us?


00:48:53.895 --> 00:48:54.979
Do what?


00:48:54.980 --> 00:48:56.106
That.


00:48:56.523 --> 00:48:59.943
Drawing freehand while the rest of us
sweat away with stencils.


00:49:01.778 --> 00:49:03.405
Are you trying to make us look bad?


00:49:04.489 --> 00:49:05.657
Why do you do it?


00:49:06.866 --> 00:49:08.451
I do it because I can.


00:49:22.465 --> 00:49:23.842
See you tomorrow, then.


00:49:46.948 --> 00:49:50.327
You can take the pencils with you
if you bring them back.


00:49:56.499 --> 00:49:59.252
In January, they're accepting
applications to the Academy of Art.


00:50:00.462 --> 00:50:02.172
I'm content with this work.


00:50:18.480 --> 00:50:19.648
What's the point of this?


00:50:20.649 --> 00:50:22.609
Does stuff like this help the workingman?


00:50:23.818 --> 00:50:26.321
Does it give your father strength
to clean the stairs?


00:50:26.946 --> 00:50:28.448
You want to help him, don't you?


00:50:29.449 --> 00:50:31.451
You even arranged for him to get the job.


00:50:36.081 --> 00:50:37.832
Been through a lot of shit, have you?


00:50:40.543 --> 00:50:42.545
But does it help to wallow in it?


00:50:42.879 --> 00:50:46.299
Will it help create a world
where your kids have it better than you?


00:50:46.675 --> 00:50:48.343
That's what communism is all about.


00:50:55.850 --> 00:50:57.686
I'll support your application.


00:50:58.812 --> 00:51:01.606
The girls at the academy
are prettier than the ones here.


00:51:33.054 --> 00:51:36.891
Can you see here
that someone left all vanity aside


00:51:37.267 --> 00:51:39.310
and put himself
in the service of the cause?


00:51:39.853 --> 00:51:41.688
In the service of the people?


00:51:43.648 --> 00:51:45.483
Work on your attitude.


00:51:45.692 --> 00:51:47.610
Work on your craft.


00:51:47.902 --> 00:51:51.489
And the right art
will flow out of you on its own accord.


00:51:52.198 --> 00:51:55.952
I would suggest Pablo Picasso
as a cautionary example.


00:51:57.078 --> 00:51:59.705
He created powerful realistic pictures


00:51:59.706 --> 00:52:03.293
that demonstrate genuine solidarity
with the working classes.


00:52:07.046 --> 00:52:12.469
But he soon slipped
into a decadent, obscene formalism.


00:52:14.012 --> 00:52:15.263
Why?


00:52:16.222 --> 00:52:20.602
Because he wanted to be seen
as an innovator, not a traditionalist.


00:52:21.686 --> 00:52:25.565
Innovation. Creative independence.
Artistic freedom.


00:52:26.441 --> 00:52:29.319
Words that initially sound tempting
to an artist.


00:52:29.986 --> 00:52:31.988
Me, me, me.


00:52:32.572 --> 00:52:36.366
But a modern artist
can only achieve real freedom


00:52:36.367 --> 00:52:39.204
if he serves the interests of the people.


00:52:39.913 --> 00:52:42.874
The "me, me, me" stance leads to misery.


00:52:43.416 --> 00:52:47.837
At best, it will lead to being subsidized
by decadent, wealthy collectors,


00:52:48.713 --> 00:52:51.673
exploiters of the workingman
who delight in the fact


00:52:51.674 --> 00:52:53.842
that they have nothing in common
with the people,


00:52:53.843 --> 00:52:55.845
not even the same taste in art.


00:52:58.515 --> 00:53:02.018
Decay, mysticism, and pornography.


00:53:03.019 --> 00:53:05.355
Empty forms, artificial constructions.


00:53:05.772 --> 00:53:08.357
Splotches, lines, spheres, cones...


00:53:08.358 --> 00:53:11.820
All that, just in order
to be considered an innovator?


00:53:13.279 --> 00:53:14.781
Yes, it's new.


00:53:15.448 --> 00:53:17.033
But it's also wrong.


00:53:18.743 --> 00:53:23.581
And vain and stupid,
undemocratic, decadent.


00:53:25.208 --> 00:53:28.545
Be different, gentlemen. Be different.


00:53:53.403 --> 00:53:55.905
You had the hammer
a little higher up before.


00:53:57.532 --> 00:53:59.367
Right, it was quite a bit higher up.


00:54:00.410 --> 00:54:01.536
Still higher.


00:54:02.620 --> 00:54:05.622
- Like this?
- The left hand was more in the middle.


00:54:05.623 --> 00:54:07.917
And your right hand
was much further to the front.


00:54:08.543 --> 00:54:10.502
- More.
- Further, further.


00:54:10.503 --> 00:54:11.879
Still further.


00:54:11.880 --> 00:54:14.423
- Like this?
- Further, further...


00:54:14.424 --> 00:54:15.967
Move the top to the front.


00:54:16.509 --> 00:54:19.052
Exactly. Right about there, huh?


00:54:19.053 --> 00:54:21.347
- That's about right.
- Looks good.


00:54:21.806 --> 00:54:23.391
No, it can't have been like that.


00:54:24.434 --> 00:54:25.894
Cut the nonsense.


00:54:26.394 --> 00:54:27.770
The hammer was higher up.


00:54:30.273 --> 00:54:32.233
No. Lower down.


00:54:33.943 --> 00:54:35.361
No, further up.


00:54:36.237 --> 00:54:37.405
Further up.


00:54:37.655 --> 00:54:41.326
Down, up, down, up.


00:54:46.581 --> 00:54:48.124
Comrade Professor!


00:54:50.126 --> 00:54:53.670
Comrade Professor,
these young people are out of control.


00:54:53.671 --> 00:54:58.176
They don't take me seriously. I have
big responsibilities here, you know!


00:55:01.137 --> 00:55:03.222
Are we in kindergarten here?


00:55:17.195 --> 00:55:18.863
Yes, it looks like we are.


00:55:47.850 --> 00:55:50.812
A girl in the Fashion Department
is giving away Western pencils!


00:55:59.654 --> 00:56:00.738
Excuse me!


00:56:03.116 --> 00:56:04.283
Excuse me!


00:56:05.785 --> 00:56:06.869
Excuse me!


00:56:09.956 --> 00:56:11.581
- Thanks.
- My pleasure.


00:56:11.582 --> 00:56:14.794
- Amazing. 2B. Thanks.
- Hello, Ernst.


00:56:16.504 --> 00:56:19.132
- Thanks for sharing.
- Of course. You're welcome.


00:56:21.217 --> 00:56:23.428
- Say hi to Lise for me.
- I will. Thanks.


00:56:24.429 --> 00:56:25.430
Michael.


00:56:26.472 --> 00:56:27.682
Thanks, Elisabeth.


00:56:31.269 --> 00:56:34.147
Don't get your hopes up. She's mine.


00:56:34.814 --> 00:56:36.607
Watch and learn.


00:56:42.280 --> 00:56:43.656
<i>2B or 4B?</i>


00:56:47.910 --> 00:56:48.953
Well?


00:56:50.329 --> 00:56:51.789
2B, but...


00:56:52.665 --> 00:56:55.793
I'd like a date even more than a pencil.


00:56:59.756 --> 00:57:01.674
Let's just leave it at a pencil for now.


00:57:02.508 --> 00:57:03.509
Are you sure?


00:57:04.343 --> 00:57:05.470
Sure.


00:57:21.069 --> 00:57:22.111
Your name's Elisabeth?


00:57:26.157 --> 00:57:27.408
Do you want one too?


00:57:27.825 --> 00:57:29.409
There's only...


00:57:29.410 --> 00:57:30.703
4B left.


00:57:37.710 --> 00:57:38.878
Thanks.


00:57:49.514 --> 00:57:52.391
A golden pheasant like you
shouldn't use a tin for an ashtray.


00:57:53.893 --> 00:57:55.144
Golden pheasant?


00:57:55.478 --> 00:57:56.479
Yes.


00:57:57.105 --> 00:57:59.023
I can't let you get away with that.


00:57:59.774 --> 00:58:01.192
I completely agree.


00:58:03.861 --> 00:58:05.154
How about a walk?


00:58:06.030 --> 00:58:07.240
In the park?


00:58:08.366 --> 00:58:10.660
So I can rectify my misapprehension?


00:58:34.267 --> 00:58:36.435
I thought you wanted to talk with me?


00:58:37.937 --> 00:58:40.148
Actually,
I wanted to take a walk with you.


00:58:41.691 --> 00:58:43.066
Very well.


00:58:43.067 --> 00:58:45.778
Then I'll make conversation.


00:58:48.906 --> 00:58:50.741
Socialist Realism,


00:58:51.409 --> 00:58:52.869
is that your thing?


00:58:54.287 --> 00:58:59.000
Probably about as much
as Lotte Ulbricht's fashion is your thing.


00:59:06.924 --> 00:59:08.843
Why do you keep looking at me like that?


00:59:10.970 --> 00:59:12.889
You remind me of somebody.


00:59:15.725 --> 00:59:17.310
Would you like to paint me?


00:59:18.102 --> 00:59:19.520
I don't know.


00:59:20.229 --> 00:59:22.315
Would you like to make a suit for me?


00:59:27.236 --> 00:59:28.654
I should be getting home.


00:59:29.488 --> 00:59:31.073
Can I accompany you?


00:59:32.575 --> 00:59:34.076
Just to the door.


00:59:40.875 --> 00:59:44.795
SOCIALISM NEEDS EVERYONE
SOCIALISM IS FOR EVERYONE


00:59:49.800 --> 00:59:52.053
DANCE SCHOOL


00:59:57.975 --> 00:59:59.393
You're taking dance lessons?


01:00:00.394 --> 01:00:01.395
I live here.


01:00:01.979 --> 01:00:03.314
The house belongs to us.


01:00:04.440 --> 01:00:07.318
You're not really dispelling
the whole golden pheasant thing.


01:00:08.778 --> 01:00:12.072
We were just lucky.
The house wasn't even hit once.


01:00:12.073 --> 01:00:14.325
The whole street looked like this
before the war.


01:00:18.913 --> 01:00:20.331
Good-bye, Kurt.


01:00:21.666 --> 01:00:22.875
Good-bye...


01:00:25.336 --> 01:00:26.587
Elisabeth?


01:00:30.758 --> 01:00:32.343
Could I call you something else?


01:00:33.302 --> 01:00:34.971
Maybe you have a nickname?


01:00:36.597 --> 01:00:38.598
Everyone calls me Elisabeth, really.


01:00:38.599 --> 01:00:41.060
"Really" mostly means
the very opposite is true.


01:00:43.479 --> 01:00:44.522
All right.


01:00:45.398 --> 01:00:47.316
My father calls me "Ellie."


01:00:49.193 --> 01:00:50.611
Good-bye, Ellie.


01:01:07.336 --> 01:01:08.546
Elisabeth.


01:02:19.200 --> 01:02:20.826
More volume.


01:02:41.097 --> 01:02:44.100
You could have taken
a bit more time off, Kurt.


01:02:47.728 --> 01:02:48.813
Good.


01:03:22.680 --> 01:03:24.348
That's enough for today.


01:03:25.933 --> 01:03:27.059
Oh, yes, good.


01:03:27.351 --> 01:03:28.436
Good night.


01:03:30.771 --> 01:03:31.856
See you tomorrow.


01:04:25.034 --> 01:04:26.869
A golden pheasant as the workingwoman?


01:04:35.669 --> 01:04:37.546
You're my semester thesis now.


01:04:39.590 --> 01:04:40.799
A suit.


01:04:41.884 --> 01:04:43.135
For you.


01:05:46.532 --> 01:05:47.908
I'll never take it off again.


01:06:16.103 --> 01:06:18.647
You're so beautiful,
it's almost unromantic.


01:06:21.066 --> 01:06:22.901
It's far too easy to love you.


01:06:28.991 --> 01:06:30.159
Do you love me?


01:06:33.245 --> 01:06:34.705
Do you love me?


01:06:36.832 --> 01:06:38.250
Otherwise it doesn't work for me.


01:06:41.337 --> 01:06:43.047
Without love, it won't work.


01:06:46.008 --> 01:06:47.509
I love you.


01:06:49.386 --> 01:06:50.679
Really?


01:06:52.389 --> 01:06:53.515
Yes.


01:07:26.048 --> 01:07:27.424
I love you!


01:07:30.511 --> 01:07:33.138
I love you.


01:07:57.538 --> 01:07:58.706
My parents!


01:08:00.082 --> 01:08:01.417
I thought they lived in Chemnitz.


01:08:02.835 --> 01:08:03.919
They do.


01:08:20.060 --> 01:08:21.186
My father!


01:08:22.104 --> 01:08:23.522
What will we do now?


01:10:55.257 --> 01:10:56.425
Elisabeth?


01:10:57.050 --> 01:10:58.260
Sound asleep.


01:10:58.719 --> 01:11:03.181
She left a candle burning.
When is she finally going to grow up?


01:11:05.559 --> 01:11:07.019
Yes, youth...


01:11:09.479 --> 01:11:11.315
So, how did you get the scratches?


01:11:12.941 --> 01:11:15.360
Like I said, it's from garden work.


01:11:16.695 --> 01:11:18.779
Yeah, I know
about that kind of garden work.


01:11:18.780 --> 01:11:21.033
Looks like you really have a green thumb.


01:11:22.576 --> 01:11:25.495
Ah, here comes the "garden work."


01:11:26.038 --> 01:11:27.164
Let's go, boys.


01:11:30.334 --> 01:11:32.752
So how are things
in your garden these days?


01:11:32.753 --> 01:11:34.463
Mine suffers from drought.


01:11:40.010 --> 01:11:42.554
Thanks for risking your life
for my reputation.


01:11:43.847 --> 01:11:45.933
But don't ever do anything so crazy again.


01:11:49.519 --> 01:11:50.645
Did your parents...


01:11:50.646 --> 01:11:53.231
They didn't notice a thing.
Nothing at all.


01:11:57.027 --> 01:11:58.487
They're moving back to Dresden.


01:11:59.738 --> 01:12:02.658
My father will get his old job back
as hospital director.


01:12:03.325 --> 01:12:05.576
But he has to rent out
a room in our house,


01:12:05.577 --> 01:12:09.581
or he'll get into trouble
with the Residence Allocation Office.


01:12:10.791 --> 01:12:12.584
He's going to put up a sign on Monday.


01:12:14.378 --> 01:12:16.046
You wouldn't perhaps like to...


01:12:17.214 --> 01:12:19.174
be the first to discover that sign?


01:12:19.591 --> 01:12:20.884
Quite by chance?


01:12:24.846 --> 01:12:28.642
They couldn't really hold it against me
if I fell in love with a tenant


01:12:29.101 --> 01:12:30.644
they chose themselves.


01:12:37.484 --> 01:12:41.154
But your mother,
won't she sense something?


01:12:42.531 --> 01:12:45.534
Oh, Mama. She's such an innocent.


01:12:46.410 --> 01:12:49.579
Don't worry about her.
She won't suspect a thing.


01:12:50.747 --> 01:12:52.374
Really, nothing at all.


01:13:18.942 --> 01:13:20.027
Yes?


01:13:20.402 --> 01:13:23.530
I've come about the sign.
ls the room still for rent?


01:13:24.656 --> 01:13:26.742
We put the sign up
a quarter of an hour ago.


01:13:27.576 --> 01:13:28.827
Is that a yes?


01:13:36.126 --> 01:13:37.209
Come in.


01:13:37.210 --> 01:13:38.711
Short, short, long.


01:13:38.712 --> 01:13:40.504
- Mrs. Seeband?
- Yes?


01:13:40.505 --> 01:13:42.548
Someone's here about the room.


01:13:42.549 --> 01:13:43.800
That was quick.


01:13:44.384 --> 01:13:47.262
Short, short and... arms up!


01:13:48.597 --> 01:13:52.934
Short, short, long. Short, short, long.


01:13:54.352 --> 01:13:57.355
Head up! Short, short, long.


01:13:58.148 --> 01:14:02.611
Short, short, long. Short, short, long.


01:14:07.866 --> 01:14:10.494
Short, short... arms up!


01:14:14.831 --> 01:14:16.249
Barnert, Kurt.


01:14:19.628 --> 01:14:21.296
What do you do for a living?


01:14:21.963 --> 01:14:23.423
I'm a student.


01:14:24.091 --> 01:14:25.382
Fashion?


01:14:25.383 --> 01:14:27.468
- Painting.
- Painting?


01:14:27.469 --> 01:14:29.345
Mrs. Hellthaler, please come up.


01:14:29.346 --> 01:14:32.557
Carl, there's a tenant for the room.
Do come down.


01:14:56.915 --> 01:14:59.459
You have facial paresis.


01:15:00.752 --> 01:15:02.379
Partial facial paralysis.


01:15:03.130 --> 01:15:04.965
The corner of your mouth hangs.


01:15:05.882 --> 01:15:09.093
Did you have an accident or Lyme disease?


01:15:09.094 --> 01:15:10.761
Kindly take this up to the office.


01:15:10.762 --> 01:15:13.181
Then my husband can talk with the tenant.


01:15:13.974 --> 01:15:17.561
My husband's a doctor. It's his passion.
Occasionally one gets a free diagnosis.


01:15:18.353 --> 01:15:19.813
You should have that examined.


01:15:20.897 --> 01:15:22.941
Kurt comes with the best recommendations.


01:15:24.234 --> 01:15:26.528
He's a student, a non-smoker...


01:15:28.029 --> 01:15:31.241
We've already agreed on the rent.


01:15:31.533 --> 01:15:34.786
But of course, it's your decision
whether he gets the room.


01:15:35.662 --> 01:15:37.288
Kurt wants to be a painter.


01:15:37.289 --> 01:15:38.415
I am a painter.


01:15:39.499 --> 01:15:41.876
The house's facade is starting to peel.


01:15:41.877 --> 01:15:43.920
Maybe we could take
the painting off the rent.


01:15:44.629 --> 01:15:47.048
I'm not that kind of painter.


01:15:48.341 --> 01:15:49.676
What kind are you?


01:15:51.261 --> 01:15:52.470
A painter of pictures.


01:15:52.762 --> 01:15:54.431
Socialist Realism?


01:15:56.183 --> 01:15:57.559
Is there any other kind?


01:15:58.768 --> 01:16:00.187
I hope not.


01:16:02.105 --> 01:16:03.857
You can have the room anyway.


01:16:05.108 --> 01:16:06.359
Thank you, Mr. Seeband.


01:16:06.693 --> 01:16:08.361
Professor Seeband, please.


01:16:14.159 --> 01:16:15.619
Nice suit.


01:17:45.333 --> 01:17:47.002
What are you doing up so late?


01:17:48.503 --> 01:17:49.838
I've... been out.


01:17:50.297 --> 01:17:51.339
Alcohol?


01:17:51.840 --> 01:17:54.092
That can't be good for your work.


01:17:54.968 --> 01:17:56.553
Now get to bed.


01:18:28.918 --> 01:18:30.628
I don't like that Kurt.


01:18:33.465 --> 01:18:36.343
We have to make sure
Ellie doesn't get too friendly with him.


01:18:40.180 --> 01:18:41.306
Why?


01:18:42.766 --> 01:18:45.060
So she can make a good catch, of course.


01:18:47.562 --> 01:18:49.564
Just as you made a good catch.


01:19:10.043 --> 01:19:14.254
Professor Seeband, about yesterday...
l... Of course, I'd never tell.


01:19:14.255 --> 01:19:16.216
You have a new subject.


01:19:18.510 --> 01:19:19.594
Me.


01:19:20.553 --> 01:19:22.347
For the directors' gallery.


01:19:23.681 --> 01:19:25.475
In that style, more or less.


01:19:26.976 --> 01:19:30.271
We start tomorrow at 4:00 p.m.
In my office at the hospital, all right?


01:19:36.194 --> 01:19:38.529
<i>Since the people of the GDR unanimously</i>


01:19:38.530 --> 01:19:41.365
<i>desire peace
and the unification of Germany,</i>


01:19:41.366 --> 01:19:44.076
<i>Prime Minister Grotewohl
presented the Bonn government...</i>


01:19:44.077 --> 01:19:46.537
The professor is coming. Please be seated.


01:19:46.538 --> 01:19:49.706
<i>...with proposals for free elections
throughout the whole of Germany.</i>


01:19:49.707 --> 01:19:52.835
<i>These proposals were rejected
by the Western occupying powers</i>


01:19:52.836 --> 01:19:54.253
<i>and the Adenauer government,</i>


01:19:54.254 --> 01:19:57.257
<i>in line with
their politics of confrontation.</i>


01:19:57.882 --> 01:20:00.467
<i>As a further consequence
of these politics,</i>


01:20:00.468 --> 01:20:04.263
<i>the government in Bonn
and the Western occupying powers</i>


01:20:04.264 --> 01:20:08.934
<i>have introduced strict border controls
at the demarcation line</i>


01:20:08.935 --> 01:20:13.105
<i>in order to emphasize their separation
from the GDR</i>


01:20:13.106 --> 01:20:16.609
<i>and thus to perpetuate
the division of Germany.</i>


01:20:32.625 --> 01:20:34.627
Thank you. Good day.


01:20:37.005 --> 01:20:38.006
Kurt.


01:20:39.174 --> 01:20:41.259
I thought you could put your easel...


01:20:42.427 --> 01:20:43.510
here.


01:20:43.511 --> 01:20:46.638
<i>The lack of any corresponding controls
at GDR borders</i>


01:20:46.639 --> 01:20:49.683
<i>has been exploited by the Western powers</i>


01:20:49.684 --> 01:20:53.103
<i>to infiltrate our sector
with an ever-increasing number of spies,</i>


01:20:53.104 --> 01:20:55.315
<i>terrorists, and smugglers.</i>


01:20:58.318 --> 01:21:02.654
<i>Until now, once their criminal activities
have been accomplished,</i>


01:21:02.655 --> 01:21:05.741
<i>they have been able to return
without any obstacle</i>


01:21:05.742 --> 01:21:09.913
<i>across the demarcation line
to West Germany.</i>


01:21:11.706 --> 01:21:17.461
<i>Consequently, we are obliged
to take measures to protect</i>


01:21:17.462 --> 01:21:19.463
<i>the peaceful interests</i>


01:21:19.464 --> 01:21:24.010
<i>of the population
of the German Democratic Republic.</i>


01:21:25.345 --> 01:21:30.475
<i>These measures have been entrusted
to the Ministry of State Security.</i>


01:21:56.668 --> 01:21:59.420
That's exactly what I had in mind.
Very good.


01:22:00.421 --> 01:22:02.215
We'll continue tomorrow at 4:00.


01:22:03.841 --> 01:22:06.302
Two sessions should be enough, right?


01:22:16.271 --> 01:22:19.107
Why are you looking
at those ancient photos again?


01:22:19.774 --> 01:22:23.278
Why does the most idiotic snapshot
have more reality than my painting?


01:22:25.613 --> 01:22:27.031
Papa likes it.


01:22:27.448 --> 01:22:28.908
That's just it.


01:22:31.286 --> 01:22:33.329
Hardly anyone likes photos of themselves.


01:22:33.955 --> 01:22:36.040
But everyone's supposed
to like a painting.


01:22:36.958 --> 01:22:38.876
So the photograph must be truer.


01:22:42.839 --> 01:22:45.133
Why did your father
go to work in Chemnitz anyway?


01:22:45.842 --> 01:22:47.885
He was the hospital director here before.


01:22:54.517 --> 01:22:56.227
He doesn't want us to talk about it.


01:23:01.274 --> 01:23:04.777
During the war, Papa treated
the wives of Goering and Goebbels.


01:23:08.948 --> 01:23:10.908
Simply because he's the best gynecologist.


01:23:12.076 --> 01:23:14.454
They traveled 200 kilometers from Berlin.


01:23:14.871 --> 01:23:18.583
As if no one there was capable
of doing a Pap smear. Just imagine!


01:23:20.627 --> 01:23:23.880
As a reward, they made him
an honorary member of the SS.


01:23:24.380 --> 01:23:25.882
He couldn't refuse.


01:23:26.799 --> 01:23:30.093
But after the war,
it was hard to explain to the Russians


01:23:30.094 --> 01:23:32.639
that he didn't have anything else
to do with the Nazis.


01:23:33.473 --> 01:23:37.644
They combed through all the archives,
but couldn't find anything against him.


01:23:47.737 --> 01:23:52.075
Today, the professor called me...
a "Willi Sitte" type of artist.


01:23:52.992 --> 01:23:55.369
But that's good. He's successful.


01:23:55.370 --> 01:23:56.788
A "Willi Sitte" type.


01:23:57.455 --> 01:23:59.332
I think I have to get out of this place.


01:24:00.833 --> 01:24:02.085
You don't mean to the West?


01:24:05.171 --> 01:24:06.673
You can't be serious.


01:24:09.550 --> 01:24:11.469
But things are going so well for us here.


01:24:15.807 --> 01:24:17.975
I could never abandon Mama.


01:24:23.731 --> 01:24:24.941
Kurt!


01:24:26.401 --> 01:24:30.362
Your diploma thesis convinced
the committee, and they chose you


01:24:30.363 --> 01:24:33.281
to paint the mural
for the new History Museum.


01:24:33.282 --> 01:24:35.785
The theme is "Unity of the Working Class."


01:24:36.703 --> 01:24:39.247
A task that even a few professors
wouldn't have minded getting.


01:24:39.956 --> 01:24:41.749
- A mural?
- Yes.


01:24:42.875 --> 01:24:44.501
But I'm not a muralist.


01:24:44.502 --> 01:24:46.671
Kurt, we both know you can do it.


01:24:48.005 --> 01:24:51.675
No, I'm sorry, it's not for me.
It's pure decoration.


01:24:51.676 --> 01:24:54.929
You'd have guaranteed work.
And even money.


01:24:56.597 --> 01:24:58.057
It's just not me.


01:25:01.602 --> 01:25:03.187
Me, me, me.


01:25:26.252 --> 01:25:28.463
No, don't move. Please.


01:25:31.048 --> 01:25:33.760
That way,
I can imagine we're a single body.


01:25:41.476 --> 01:25:42.977
I'm pregnant.


01:25:46.981 --> 01:25:48.900
Then you belong to me completely now.


01:25:52.403 --> 01:25:54.530
You belong with me, I mean.


01:26:05.416 --> 01:26:07.335
We have to tell them, Ellie.


01:26:19.555 --> 01:26:21.933
Maybe we should tell them
we're together first.


01:26:23.184 --> 01:26:25.478
To split the shock up into small parts.


01:26:28.439 --> 01:26:30.900
I think your mother
already suspects something.


01:26:35.112 --> 01:26:37.240
It's not Mama I'm worried about.


01:26:38.741 --> 01:26:40.743
It'll hit Papa completely out of the blue.


01:26:42.787 --> 01:26:45.122
For him, I'll always be 12 years old.


01:26:54.465 --> 01:26:55.967
I think Ellie's pregnant.


01:27:00.805 --> 01:27:01.848
What?


01:27:02.390 --> 01:27:05.016
The temperature of her hand
has been slightly elevated,


01:27:05.017 --> 01:27:06.978
but she shows no symptoms of a cold.


01:27:07.812 --> 01:27:11.148
Yesterday she left the room
twice at dinner,


01:27:11.732 --> 01:27:14.067
didn't touch her porridge at breakfast,


01:27:14.068 --> 01:27:17.363
and grabbed the chair for support
when she got up.


01:27:18.406 --> 01:27:20.074
Third month, I'd say.


01:27:21.742 --> 01:27:23.201
Maybe the fourth.


01:27:23.202 --> 01:27:25.329
My God, she's still a child herself!


01:27:26.247 --> 01:27:29.000
The problem isn't her age, but the man.


01:27:30.293 --> 01:27:31.586
But who could it be?


01:27:34.881 --> 01:27:37.299
Leptosomic, melancholic,


01:27:37.300 --> 01:27:40.928
son of a man who took his life
because he had to clean a few stairs.


01:27:42.054 --> 01:27:44.974
My father would've called
a man like that a "dead loss."


01:27:46.559 --> 01:27:49.478
This is not the genetic material
I want for our descendants.


01:27:50.104 --> 01:27:51.647
We have to prevent it.


01:27:53.983 --> 01:27:55.151
But how?


01:27:57.069 --> 01:28:00.364
After 30 years as a gynecologist,
I can tell you one thing.


01:28:01.157 --> 01:28:04.952
An abortion has been known
to end almost any dalliance.


01:29:16.607 --> 01:29:20.111
No, I don't know that one.
What's the difference?


01:29:21.153 --> 01:29:24.156
The psychotic
thinks two and two makes five,


01:29:24.532 --> 01:29:27.952
while the neurotic
knows two and two make four.


01:29:28.536 --> 01:29:30.121
But it worries him.


01:29:38.212 --> 01:29:41.006
There's something we want to tell you.


01:29:41.007 --> 01:29:44.176
About the Academy of Art?
I'm always interested in that.


01:29:44.593 --> 01:29:47.972
No. Although it's also about the academy.


01:29:48.723 --> 01:29:51.976
Kurt has been commissioned
to paint the mural in the History Museum.


01:29:53.060 --> 01:29:54.728
Painting walls, after all?


01:29:54.729 --> 01:29:58.024
The mural's theme
is "Unity of the Working Class."


01:29:59.150 --> 01:30:01.985
And on the subject of unity...


01:30:01.986 --> 01:30:03.404
What is it, my child?


01:30:04.447 --> 01:30:06.615
Nothing unpleasant, I hope.


01:30:07.867 --> 01:30:09.493
My nerves, you know.


01:30:11.328 --> 01:30:12.413
We...


01:30:13.748 --> 01:30:15.750
We're... together.


01:30:17.126 --> 01:30:19.462
You're working on the mural too?


01:30:21.213 --> 01:30:24.133
We're a couple.
We have been for some time.


01:30:25.134 --> 01:30:27.094
A couple of students?


01:30:28.971 --> 01:30:30.723
A couple in a loving relationship.


01:30:33.559 --> 01:30:36.937
- And there's something else.
- That's big news.


01:30:37.521 --> 01:30:40.565
Yes, and as well as that...


01:30:40.566 --> 01:30:42.902
My God, I need to digest this first.


01:30:47.907 --> 01:30:50.242
This is so totally unexpected.


01:30:51.619 --> 01:30:53.746
Please bring the professor some water!


01:30:56.874 --> 01:30:58.375
Thank you.


01:31:27.988 --> 01:31:30.074
I'm happy you told us


01:31:31.033 --> 01:31:32.535
and told us early.


01:31:34.328 --> 01:31:37.206
There's something about Ellie
you need to know.


01:31:39.667 --> 01:31:42.545
We didn't want
to worry Ellie unnecessarily,


01:31:43.170 --> 01:31:46.006
so we never
really fully explained it to her,


01:31:46.340 --> 01:31:47.508
but...


01:31:49.468 --> 01:31:53.888
As a little girl, Ellie had
a serious infection of the pelvis.


01:31:53.889 --> 01:31:56.474
It left scar tissue in the fallopian tubes


01:31:56.475 --> 01:31:59.019
and caused considerable cilia damage.


01:32:00.146 --> 01:32:01.230
Cilia?


01:32:01.522 --> 01:32:04.190
Cilia are the tiny hairs
in the mucus of the fallopian tubes


01:32:04.191 --> 01:32:07.236
which transport
the fertilized egg to the uterus.


01:32:09.572 --> 01:32:14.243
We've been looking for a way
to correct her condition surgically.


01:32:16.453 --> 01:32:17.663
But if she...


01:32:18.789 --> 01:32:21.375
were to become pregnant
before we find one,


01:32:22.293 --> 01:32:25.545
she'd be at an extreme risk
of having an extrauterine gravidity,


01:32:25.546 --> 01:32:27.882
an ectopic pregnancy.


01:32:28.883 --> 01:32:30.843
A tubal pregnancy.


01:32:31.719 --> 01:32:34.680
This could lead
to severe internal bleeding.


01:32:37.057 --> 01:32:39.560
So I have to warn you...


01:32:40.561 --> 01:32:42.979
though not for the same reason


01:32:42.980 --> 01:32:45.566
that fathers normally warn men
pursuing their daughters,


01:32:46.150 --> 01:32:50.696
not to become intimate with her
until we've relieved this condition.


01:32:51.071 --> 01:32:53.324
A pregnancy at this point in time...


01:32:54.325 --> 01:32:56.410
could be life-threatening for Ellie.


01:33:03.667 --> 01:33:06.754
You do understand? Life-threatening.


01:33:17.473 --> 01:33:19.308
And if she were pregnant already?


01:33:23.520 --> 01:33:25.481
Then I'd have to examine her immediately.


01:33:54.885 --> 01:33:56.470
I must act immediately.


01:33:57.346 --> 01:34:00.808
The pregnancy is considerably
more advanced than I feared.


01:34:01.225 --> 01:34:02.977
It's already the third month.


01:34:07.606 --> 01:34:08.816
An abortion?


01:34:09.275 --> 01:34:13.195
If I don't remove the fetus immediately,
she won't survive the pregnancy.


01:34:14.196 --> 01:34:15.364
Here?


01:34:17.032 --> 01:34:18.951
We have a reputation to uphold.


01:34:21.662 --> 01:34:23.414
Is it really the only way?


01:34:23.998 --> 01:34:25.164
Really?


01:34:25.165 --> 01:34:27.167
Do you doubt my professional ability?


01:34:28.043 --> 01:34:29.795
Would I subject myself to this,


01:34:30.254 --> 01:34:32.715
and my daughter,
if it were not absolutely necessary?


01:35:24.266 --> 01:35:27.102
He had an SS uniform tailor-made.


01:35:29.271 --> 01:35:33.317
For hours he would change positions
in front of the mirror...


01:35:34.818 --> 01:35:37.404
<i>trying different poses
to find the best one.</i>


01:35:39.656 --> 01:35:41.784
<i>He didn't care that I could see him.</i>


01:35:44.828 --> 01:35:46.246
<i>I was just a little girl.</i>


01:35:57.674 --> 01:36:00.219
<i>There was a skull on his cap.</i>


01:36:01.970 --> 01:36:02.971
<i>In silver.</i>


01:36:04.598 --> 01:36:05.974
<i>A skull.</i>


01:36:13.899 --> 01:36:16.068
<i>A doctor is supposed to heal people.</i>


01:36:18.570 --> 01:36:20.406
He's supposed to heal.


01:36:26.412 --> 01:36:28.914
Am I always going to be at his mercy?


01:36:33.001 --> 01:36:35.711
...a gifted doctor, a humanist,


01:36:35.712 --> 01:36:39.340
an active co-creator
of our Socialist Republic.


01:36:39.341 --> 01:36:44.220
And a fine example
for all members of his profession.


01:36:44.221 --> 01:36:48.766
For these reasons, today,
December 11, the GDR's Health Care Day,


01:36:48.767 --> 01:36:51.311
I'm proud to present him
with the Robert Koch Medal


01:36:51.645 --> 01:36:56.275
and the title
"Distinguished Doctor of the People."


01:37:11.790 --> 01:37:15.836
Thank you, Comrade Minister,
for the kind words, which I don't deserve.


01:37:16.170 --> 01:37:20.424
As a doctor and a member of society,
I am merely doing my duty.


01:37:21.216 --> 01:37:25.429
I'm simply a cog in the huge machine
of the international socialist movement.


01:37:26.513 --> 01:37:28.431
Just as the painter


01:37:28.432 --> 01:37:32.311
of this far too flattering portrait of me
is only a small cog,


01:37:32.811 --> 01:37:37.024
his style indistinguishable
from the other painters here.


01:37:37.608 --> 01:37:41.445
As all are just small cogs
in a large apparatus,


01:37:41.862 --> 01:37:47.326
which with the help of the Soviet Union
is heading steadily towards a joint goal...


01:37:47.743 --> 01:37:49.118
Communism.


01:37:49.119 --> 01:37:50.120
Thank you.


01:38:32.538 --> 01:38:33.997
What did he want?


01:38:35.749 --> 01:38:39.169
I'm to report to KGB headquarters
tomorrow. That's all he said.


01:38:47.970 --> 01:38:51.932
Looks like that plan didn't work either.
They're even closer than before.


01:38:53.475 --> 01:38:54.935
Patience, Martha.


01:38:55.644 --> 01:38:57.062
Just a bit of patience.


01:39:26.466 --> 01:39:29.135
General Murawjow,
Professor Seeband, as per your orders.


01:39:29.136 --> 01:39:30.596
You may go.


01:39:41.773 --> 01:39:42.858
Carl!


01:39:49.865 --> 01:39:50.991
Carl.


01:39:52.326 --> 01:39:55.037
Wait, I want to show you something.


01:40:05.380 --> 01:40:06.673
Come and sit down.


01:40:17.267 --> 01:40:20.020
Carl, I'm being transferred.


01:40:20.771 --> 01:40:22.230
Back to Moscow.


01:40:23.148 --> 01:40:25.442
I won't be able to protect you any longer.


01:40:26.360 --> 01:40:28.654
All the others have been captured.


01:40:29.237 --> 01:40:31.365
We are still hunting for Burghart Kroll


01:40:31.823 --> 01:40:37.244
and the "medical coordinator
of the Dresden region


01:40:37.245 --> 01:40:42.626
for the euthanasia program,"
who is still officially unknown.


01:40:43.126 --> 01:40:46.295
I can't guarantee that my successor


01:40:46.296 --> 01:40:50.300
won't question doctors
and nurses again in this matter.


01:40:51.718 --> 01:40:55.347
You should leave the country as well
and never come back.


01:40:55.847 --> 01:40:59.518
Apply for an emigration permit
for you and your wife.


01:41:00.268 --> 01:41:02.229
It will be approved.


01:41:03.105 --> 01:41:06.358
No one will suspect the truth in the West.


01:41:07.776 --> 01:41:10.445
Let's hope our side doesn't, either.


01:41:14.825 --> 01:41:15.909
Carl.


01:41:18.829 --> 01:41:22.749
You can't tell me anything about Kroll?


01:41:24.793 --> 01:41:26.169
Where he is?


01:41:27.671 --> 01:41:30.632
Who else was at your meetings?


01:41:34.845 --> 01:41:37.764
You'd be helping me a great deal.


01:41:43.061 --> 01:41:44.730
I never met the man.


01:41:45.647 --> 01:41:47.149
I don't know anything about him.


01:42:01.580 --> 01:42:05.792
We shall never meet again, my friend.


01:42:07.002 --> 01:42:10.172
I hope I have repaid my debt.


01:42:22.893 --> 01:42:24.144
You may go.


01:42:30.567 --> 01:42:33.111
Dear Ellie, dear Kurt.


01:42:34.529 --> 01:42:37.616
So now you have been
my son-in-law for two hours.


01:42:38.450 --> 01:42:40.534
I'll be leaving my daughter in your hands


01:42:40.535 --> 01:42:43.246
when we leave the GDR
at the end of the month.


01:42:44.998 --> 01:42:48.210
There is only one thing I'd like
to tell you for your life's journey.


01:42:49.544 --> 01:42:52.464
It's not enough to be "good."


01:42:53.715 --> 01:42:56.967
I've seen many men who were just "good"


01:42:56.968 --> 01:43:00.764
be passed over, dispossessed,
even eradicated.


01:43:03.016 --> 01:43:05.685
If you want security in this world,


01:43:06.061 --> 01:43:09.564
no matter what you do,
you have to be the best.


01:43:10.565 --> 01:43:12.275
Not one of the best.


01:43:13.693 --> 01:43:15.195
The best.


01:43:17.447 --> 01:43:18.740
To the married couple!


01:43:19.991 --> 01:43:21.159
Cheers.


01:43:28.542 --> 01:43:29.668
Cheers.


01:43:32.671 --> 01:43:36.382
"...thus I'm now in Oldenburg,
in the Sanderbusch Clinic,


01:43:36.383 --> 01:43:40.971
with every prospect of taking charge
when Erkner retires two years from now.


01:43:41.638 --> 01:43:44.850
Take care of yourself, your Papa."


01:43:45.892 --> 01:43:48.270
It looks as though
he's landed on his feet again.


01:44:33.189 --> 01:44:35.358
How much would you give me
for the Wartburg?


01:44:35.984 --> 01:44:37.152
Are you out of your mind?


01:44:37.777 --> 01:44:40.737
Do you know how long an ordinary mortal
has to wait to get a car like that?


01:44:41.364 --> 01:44:43.199
I just don't like it anymore.


01:44:45.493 --> 01:44:46.494
300 marks?


01:44:50.874 --> 01:44:53.960
Kurt.
They don't even paint anymore in the West.


01:44:55.587 --> 01:44:57.172
They consider painting bourgeois.


01:44:58.423 --> 01:45:01.343
Don't they find "bourgeois" good?


01:45:02.052 --> 01:45:03.720
Oh, what do I know?


01:45:06.139 --> 01:45:09.225
Of course we all want to get rid of you.
Of course.


01:45:10.185 --> 01:45:11.810
But you've got a life here.


01:45:11.811 --> 01:45:15.106
You have money. You're becoming famous.


01:45:15.732 --> 01:45:19.569
I mean, girls have gone to bed with me
because I'm your assistant.


01:45:20.487 --> 01:45:22.864
You can handle the apparatchiks
like nobody else.


01:45:24.032 --> 01:45:26.952
You're about to turn 30,
not that young anymore.


01:45:27.535 --> 01:45:28.536
You're...


01:45:29.537 --> 01:45:30.580
Why?


01:45:31.247 --> 01:45:32.624
Because none of that matters.


01:45:33.416 --> 01:45:34.668
Then what does matter?


01:45:36.503 --> 01:45:37.879
The truth.


01:45:39.381 --> 01:45:41.007
And who says what's true?


01:45:41.758 --> 01:45:44.010
Me, me, me.


01:45:57.565 --> 01:45:58.566
260?


01:45:59.109 --> 01:46:00.110
Fine.


01:46:05.448 --> 01:46:06.658
Do you need canvases?


01:46:07.534 --> 01:46:08.701
You've got some?


01:46:08.702 --> 01:46:11.036
In my studio, with pictures on them.


01:46:11.037 --> 01:46:12.122
What?


01:46:12.831 --> 01:46:16.292
Paint over all of them, please.
I never want to see them again.


01:46:17.627 --> 01:46:19.963
Believe me,
nothing I've ever painted is right.


01:46:23.633 --> 01:46:27.720
- ...the idea of Socialist Realism.
- Visit from Normannenstraße.


01:46:27.721 --> 01:46:29.305
What about the murals?


01:46:30.348 --> 01:46:31.641
You can't destroy them.


01:46:31.933 --> 01:46:34.185
...depicted as an unstoppable train.


01:46:41.276 --> 01:46:43.277
Comrades, were you in charge of...


01:46:43.278 --> 01:46:45.154
Other people
will take care of that for me.


01:46:45.155 --> 01:46:46.865
We've been here right from the start


01:46:47.532 --> 01:46:50.994
and can testify that
all involved have impeccable views.


01:46:52.662 --> 01:46:55.415
MARCH 13, 1961


01:46:58.043 --> 01:47:01.046
BERLIN FRIEDRICHSTRAßE STATION


01:47:43.880 --> 01:47:45.548
Stop. Stay there!


01:47:50.386 --> 01:47:51.595
What's in that suitcase?


01:47:51.596 --> 01:47:55.058
Those are things
that belong to my brother-in-law.


01:48:13.618 --> 01:48:17.372
<i>Incoming train to Zoologischer Garten.</i>


01:48:21.459 --> 01:48:22.919
<i>Stand back, please.</i>


01:48:34.013 --> 01:48:35.682
They make it almost too easy.


01:48:36.516 --> 01:48:37.809
Not for much longer.


01:48:40.937 --> 01:48:43.648
<i>Next station, Zoologischer Garten.</i>


01:49:06.129 --> 01:49:08.380
- Your name?
- Barnert, Kurt.


01:49:08.381 --> 01:49:09.632
Please fill this out.


01:49:10.216 --> 01:49:12.927
Your beds are over there.
I'll come to you.


01:49:14.179 --> 01:49:16.723
Mrs. Müller? Mrs. Müller!


01:49:31.696 --> 01:49:33.406
- Thank you.
- Good day.


01:49:38.995 --> 01:49:40.288
- There you go.
- Thank you.


01:50:33.633 --> 01:50:34.884
<i>Dear Professor.</i>


01:50:35.927 --> 01:50:38.429
<i>By the time you read this,
I shall be in the West.</i>


01:50:39.472 --> 01:50:44.102
<i>I couldn't talk to you about it before. It
would've involved you in a criminal act.</i>


01:50:45.186 --> 01:50:47.187
<i>You were always very good to me,</i>


01:50:47.188 --> 01:50:50.816
<i>so I hope you will believe me
when I tell you</i>


01:50:50.817 --> 01:50:52.777
<i>that I haven't made this decision lightly.</i>


01:51:57.842 --> 01:51:59.344
Hello. I'm Kurt.


01:52:00.636 --> 01:52:01.846
Should I come back later?


01:52:02.096 --> 01:52:03.264
No, come in.


01:52:04.265 --> 01:52:05.433
Klaus, stay still.


01:52:07.352 --> 01:52:10.021
You'll spoil your father's
birthday present for Mommy.


01:52:17.612 --> 01:52:18.821
How old are you again?


01:52:19.238 --> 01:52:21.741
Twenty-nine. Almost 30.


01:52:22.450 --> 01:52:23.743
You look younger.


01:52:29.457 --> 01:52:31.625
As I said, Munich's a good idea.


01:52:31.626 --> 01:52:35.879
People there have plenty of money and
constantly need portraits and landscapes.


01:52:35.880 --> 01:52:37.215
The same goes for Hamburg.


01:52:39.425 --> 01:52:42.428
What I'd advise you against is Dusseldorf.


01:52:43.388 --> 01:52:44.555
Dusseldorf?


01:52:45.556 --> 01:52:48.476
It's all modern art there.
You know, avant-garde.


01:52:49.143 --> 01:52:52.020
If you didn't study at their academy,
you don't stand a chance.


01:52:52.021 --> 01:52:53.231
It's a kind of mafia.


01:52:54.482 --> 01:52:56.109
Munich is good.


01:52:56.734 --> 01:52:58.611
Hamburg is good.


01:52:59.112 --> 01:53:01.072
Berlin is middling.


01:53:02.115 --> 01:53:03.533
As you can see for yourself.


01:53:03.950 --> 01:53:05.118
Klaus, stay still.


01:53:18.256 --> 01:53:20.590
DUSSELDORF ART ACADEMY
OPEN HOUSE


01:53:20.591 --> 01:53:23.803
Good day. My name is Kurt Barnert.


01:53:24.262 --> 01:53:26.431
I called about a guided tour.


01:53:43.823 --> 01:53:46.576
He punched him in the nose
in the middle of the lecture.


01:53:49.036 --> 01:53:51.663
He gave the Hitler salute!


01:53:51.664 --> 01:53:55.042
- Claimed it was just a provocation.
- How tasteless!


01:53:55.751 --> 01:53:58.628
...paid 9,000 marks for a lump of soil.


01:53:58.629 --> 01:53:59.796
Unbelievable!


01:53:59.797 --> 01:54:01.382
You're still under 26, I hope?


01:54:03.968 --> 01:54:05.386
Good, and what do you want to do?


01:54:06.053 --> 01:54:08.347
Performances? Installations? Sculpture?


01:54:08.973 --> 01:54:11.809
- Well, to be honest, painting.
- "Painting"?


01:54:14.103 --> 01:54:18.607
No offense, I'm from the East myself.
Mecklenburg. Harry, Harry Preußer.


01:54:18.608 --> 01:54:19.650
Kurt.


01:54:20.818 --> 01:54:23.029
Nobody here paints anymore.


01:54:24.822 --> 01:54:27.825
People want something new. An idea.


01:54:47.595 --> 01:54:50.472
- An idea?
- Yes. But not something like that.


01:54:50.473 --> 01:54:53.392
Something new,
or at least in new packaging.


01:54:54.936 --> 01:54:59.022
Like Yves Klein, who says,
"I'm claiming ultramarine for myself.


01:54:59.023 --> 01:55:00.399
I'm even going to patent it.


01:55:00.983 --> 01:55:04.361
It's now called Yves Klein Blue.
I'll only express myself in it.


01:55:04.362 --> 01:55:07.573
I'll paint the breasts
of a beautiful woman with Yves Klein Blue.


01:55:08.241 --> 01:55:11.993
She'll smear the paint
on the breasts of another beautiful woman.


01:55:11.994 --> 01:55:15.623
I'll paint sponges with Yves Klein Blue
and use it to stick them to canvases."


01:55:24.423 --> 01:55:26.743
Of course, it's no good
if someone else had the idea first.


01:55:27.843 --> 01:55:30.471
Lucio Fontana's been slashing
canvases for six years.


01:55:31.430 --> 01:55:33.975
But Katrin is hot as hell,
so she can do whatever she likes.


01:55:42.400 --> 01:55:44.902
Let us focus not on


01:55:45.736 --> 01:55:48.155
what is obvious,
but on things more spurious.


01:55:48.698 --> 01:55:50.575
Let profoundness emerge.


01:55:51.033 --> 01:55:52.785
That's Adrian Schimmel.


01:55:53.953 --> 01:55:55.663
The name says it all... "Adrian Mold."


01:55:56.622 --> 01:55:59.583
His real name is Adrian Finck,
son of the Mannesmann CEO.


01:55:59.584 --> 01:56:02.962
A little snot.
But he can talk, that's for sure.


01:56:04.380 --> 01:56:06.340
But is the wallpaper idea enough?


01:56:07.675 --> 01:56:10.761
To put it differently, what does
the entire composition say to you?


01:56:12.430 --> 01:56:14.681
Yes, I think it's very nice.


01:56:14.682 --> 01:56:19.186
But it's still what you might call...
wallpaper.


01:56:19.645 --> 01:56:21.480
- I'm so sorry.
- Yes.


01:56:22.064 --> 01:56:23.065
Yes.


01:56:23.608 --> 01:56:25.943
But you see, it only looks that way.


01:56:26.444 --> 01:56:28.862
That's what we artists are searching for.


01:56:28.863 --> 01:56:31.407
What's hidden behind the decorative.


01:56:32.074 --> 01:56:35.411
Look.
The emptiness, expressed by the white,


01:56:35.703 --> 01:56:37.538
which I placed between the stencils.


01:56:37.955 --> 01:56:39.497
The banality


01:56:39.498 --> 01:56:42.543
represented by the recurring pattern
I applied to my work.


01:56:43.169 --> 01:56:46.297
The senseless stridency
visible in the neon colors.


01:56:46.756 --> 01:56:48.758
That's exactly what has brought you here.


01:56:49.884 --> 01:56:54.138
You have a deep sense of the artistic.
Otherwise you wouldn't have ended up here.


01:56:54.889 --> 01:56:56.891
Your friends see pretty wallpaper.


01:56:57.391 --> 01:56:59.143
You see the dimension behind it.


01:56:59.727 --> 01:57:00.853
Wonderful.


01:57:02.480 --> 01:57:03.606
And...


01:57:04.565 --> 01:57:07.193
is it possible to purchase
something like this?


01:57:09.654 --> 01:57:12.657
It is.
That's what's so magnificent about art.


01:57:16.535 --> 01:57:20.164
Money makes money. You know how it goes.


01:57:20.581 --> 01:57:23.376
But an artist shouldn't have
to talk about his work like that.


01:57:23.876 --> 01:57:28.129
He wants to prove to his successful family
that he's a success even without them.


01:57:28.130 --> 01:57:29.757
Money is all that counts for them.


01:57:31.133 --> 01:57:35.262
I want to prove to my unsuccessful family
that I'm a success in spite of them.


01:57:35.721 --> 01:57:37.431
Money is all that counts there, too.


01:57:37.765 --> 01:57:39.684
Families. What a load of crap!


01:57:44.105 --> 01:57:47.857
But you must be 26 at most
when you have the idea, or forget it!


01:57:47.858 --> 01:57:49.109
Why?


01:57:49.110 --> 01:57:53.072
Just think. Picasso was 26 when he painted
Les <i>Demoiselles</i> d'Avignon.


01:57:53.572 --> 01:57:57.158
Duchamp was 25 when he painted
<i>Nude Descending</i> a Staircase.


01:57:57.159 --> 01:57:59.495
And Michelangelo was 24
when he did the Pietà.


01:58:00.496 --> 01:58:02.289
- Good-bye.
- Good-bye.


01:58:04.792 --> 01:58:07.252
- What do you call it?
- Potato Pendulum.


01:58:07.253 --> 01:58:08.546
No more dots?


01:58:09.213 --> 01:58:11.173
I'm more interested in potatoes now.


01:58:12.883 --> 01:58:15.636
This is Kurt. He's from the East, too.
Wants to study here.


01:58:17.221 --> 01:58:20.558
I guess you've already had to listen
to Harry's speech about "the idea"?


01:58:20.975 --> 01:58:22.309
You don't believe it?


01:58:23.060 --> 01:58:24.540
I'm really much more interested in...


01:58:25.938 --> 01:58:27.022
potatoes.


01:58:28.065 --> 01:58:29.650
Come on, before you get corrupted.


01:58:34.447 --> 01:58:35.905
<i>Arendt No.</i>


01:58:35.906 --> 01:58:37.450
What he wants, nobody knows.


01:58:38.033 --> 01:58:39.659
He used to do everything


01:58:39.660 --> 01:58:43.329
in big dots, all the same color,
that he printed on boards.


01:58:43.330 --> 01:58:44.874
Could have been a real idea.


01:58:45.332 --> 01:58:46.459
And now that.


01:58:46.917 --> 01:58:49.545
In two months, it'll be something
completely different again.


01:58:53.883 --> 01:58:55.217
Our professor...


01:58:56.469 --> 01:58:59.430
Antonius van Verten.
Guess you've heard of him, even in Saxony.


01:59:01.932 --> 01:59:03.058
A true original.


01:59:03.684 --> 01:59:06.228
Though I'm sure
he'd prefer the term "legend."


01:59:06.687 --> 01:59:07.980
He always wears that hat.


01:59:10.149 --> 01:59:13.694
One time a very pretty student seduced
him, just to see him without the hat.


01:59:15.446 --> 01:59:17.156
He kept it on, even in bed.


01:59:21.202 --> 01:59:23.078
Only works with felt and grease.


01:59:23.621 --> 01:59:24.705
And Why?


01:59:25.498 --> 01:59:28.334
That remains his big, legendary secret.


01:59:30.044 --> 01:59:33.339
We have to go to all his lectures,
but he never looks at anything we do.


01:59:34.423 --> 01:59:37.343
He says you're the only one
who knows if you're doing it right.


01:59:37.760 --> 01:59:39.720
I think he simply doesn't care about us.


01:59:40.554 --> 01:59:42.431
Well, we don't care about him either.


01:59:43.432 --> 01:59:45.850
But whether you're accepted,
or get a studio,


01:59:45.851 --> 01:59:48.145
it's all completely up to that maniac.


01:59:51.106 --> 01:59:53.108
Come on, he's not really that interesting.


01:59:56.320 --> 01:59:59.824
BARNERT, KURT. AGE 26.


02:00:03.118 --> 02:00:04.954
You haven't submitted a portfolio.


02:00:05.913 --> 02:00:07.665
I couldn't bring anything with me.


02:00:08.707 --> 02:00:10.167
What have you done up to now?


02:00:12.086 --> 02:00:13.128
Painting.


02:00:13.504 --> 02:00:15.506
- In East Germany?
- Yes.


02:00:16.215 --> 02:00:18.050
Socialist Realism.


02:00:21.804 --> 02:00:25.056
WALL SURROUNDS EAST BERLIN!
TEAR GAS AND TANKS


02:00:25.057 --> 02:00:27.643
So now they really have built a wall.


02:00:29.144 --> 02:00:30.354
Did you feel that coming?


02:00:33.440 --> 02:00:37.069
"Nobody has the intention."
It usually means the opposite is true.


02:00:40.114 --> 02:00:43.075
But somehow it's almost art, that wall.


02:00:44.451 --> 02:00:46.704
A piece of landscape art.


02:00:47.288 --> 02:00:49.790
The craftsmanship involved is secondary.


02:00:50.291 --> 02:00:52.418
Hundreds of thousands
have a problem with it.


02:00:53.502 --> 02:00:55.462
Consistent German madness.


02:01:00.885 --> 02:01:02.970
What do you like in art?


02:01:10.936 --> 02:01:12.897
Don't like talking about yourself, do you?


02:01:15.858 --> 02:01:18.611
But your eyes tell me
that you've seen more than any of us.


02:01:26.869 --> 02:01:28.704
GRANTED ADMISSION


02:01:31.749 --> 02:01:32.875
STUDIO SPACE


02:01:34.001 --> 02:01:36.962
These are the only conditions for you,
like everyone else.


02:01:37.421 --> 02:01:40.466
That you come to the lectures.


02:01:41.216 --> 02:01:43.760
And that you never ask me


02:01:43.761 --> 02:01:47.848
to look at anything you do.


02:01:51.602 --> 02:01:52.811
Agreed?


02:01:54.980 --> 02:01:57.900
In any case, you're the only one
who knows if it's good or not.


02:02:18.003 --> 02:02:20.464
One step forward, two steps back.


02:02:21.006 --> 02:02:22.216
Oh, come on.


02:02:23.092 --> 02:02:25.636
You can do anything you like here.


02:02:26.595 --> 02:02:28.597
If I only knew what that was.


02:02:37.523 --> 02:02:38.691
SPD?


02:02:39.108 --> 02:02:40.984
PROSPERITY FOR ALL!


02:02:40.985 --> 02:02:42.318
NO EXPERIMENTS!


02:02:42.319 --> 02:02:43.654
CDU?


02:02:44.113 --> 02:02:46.489
- Who will you vote for?
- CDU!


02:02:46.490 --> 02:02:48.574
- FDP!
- German Peace Union!


02:02:48.575 --> 02:02:49.993
They're criminals.


02:02:49.994 --> 02:02:52.413
- As if they'd do it any better.
- SPD!


02:02:52.830 --> 02:02:54.373
Don't vote for anyone.


02:02:55.916 --> 02:02:57.710
Never vote for another party again.


02:02:58.627 --> 02:02:59.837
Vote for art.


02:03:00.713 --> 02:03:02.423
It's either-or.


02:03:04.216 --> 02:03:07.011
In art only, freedom is not an illusion.


02:03:08.262 --> 02:03:11.432
After the Nazi catastrophe,
only the artist can give people


02:03:11.890 --> 02:03:14.184
back their sense of freedom.


02:03:15.269 --> 02:03:18.022
Every individual,
whether he's a garbage man


02:03:18.731 --> 02:03:22.568
or a farmer,
has the chance to be an artist...


02:03:23.610 --> 02:03:28.407
if he develops his own subjective
abilities without external guidelines.


02:03:29.074 --> 02:03:30.826
If you aren't free...


02:03:31.994 --> 02:03:35.247
completely free, then nobody else will be.


02:03:36.248 --> 02:03:40.127
By making yourselves free,
you are liberating the world.


02:03:41.420 --> 02:03:43.297
You are priests.


02:03:44.298 --> 02:03:45.924
You are revolutionaries.


02:03:46.633 --> 02:03:48.135
You are liberators.


02:03:50.471 --> 02:03:52.306
Make your burnt offerings!


02:05:01.125 --> 02:05:03.335
Don't tell me you've joined the slashers.


02:05:23.188 --> 02:05:24.773
That's almost an idea.


02:05:25.983 --> 02:05:27.109
You learn fast.


02:07:55.966 --> 02:07:57.592
I lost it.


02:08:17.946 --> 02:08:19.448
I went to see the doctor.


02:08:19.948 --> 02:08:21.992
I won't be able to have children.


02:08:26.788 --> 02:08:28.749
And you know what he said?


02:08:30.917 --> 02:08:32.461
It was the abortion.


02:08:33.253 --> 02:08:34.838
Not cilia damage.


02:08:37.549 --> 02:08:39.801
The supporting structures
have been damaged.


02:08:41.678 --> 02:08:43.764
"Cervical insufficiency."


02:08:46.266 --> 02:08:48.685
We're never going to make it
past the third month.


02:08:54.816 --> 02:08:57.069
Because he wanted to keep it so pure...


02:08:58.653 --> 02:09:01.490
he only succeeded in extinguishing
his own bloodline.


02:09:10.707 --> 02:09:13.168
We won't have any children, Kurt.


02:09:31.395 --> 02:09:32.813
Your pictures...


02:09:33.522 --> 02:09:36.066
Your pictures have to be our children,
okay?


02:09:40.904 --> 02:09:42.364
Good.


02:10:11.184 --> 02:10:12.310
Yes...


02:10:14.729 --> 02:10:18.066
Last time we went over...


02:10:22.821 --> 02:10:24.781
No.No, no.


02:10:39.463 --> 02:10:42.007
Have you all studied Lehmbruck?


02:10:46.261 --> 02:10:48.346
Better to look at this with the episcope.


02:10:57.147 --> 02:10:58.773
So, Lehmbruck.


02:10:59.941 --> 02:11:05.363
He said that each work of art must retain
something from the first days of Creation.


02:11:06.198 --> 02:11:07.324
As if...


02:11:13.914 --> 02:11:15.916
Almost as if it were still divine...


02:11:17.167 --> 02:11:18.835
As if it were only just emerging...


02:11:20.170 --> 02:11:24.049
from the primeval mass, from the rib...


02:11:25.926 --> 02:11:26.968
No.


02:11:27.886 --> 02:11:30.012
No, a different approach.


02:11:30.013 --> 02:11:34.058
Has anyone had an insight this week?


02:11:34.059 --> 02:11:35.435
A realization...


02:11:37.020 --> 02:11:39.147
you'd perhaps like to share?


02:11:48.532 --> 02:11:49.908
Lottery numbers.


02:11:52.327 --> 02:11:55.497
No, really. The lottery numbers.


02:11:57.040 --> 02:11:59.459
If I tell you six numbers at random...


02:11:59.751 --> 02:12:06.006
5, 7, 23, 29, 44, 11...


02:12:06.007 --> 02:12:08.343
that's just stupid.


02:12:09.302 --> 02:12:12.722
But if I read you the winning numbers
from the lottery...


02:12:13.265 --> 02:12:14.558
May I?


02:12:19.312 --> 02:12:26.312
"2, 17, 19, 25, 45, 48."


02:12:28.113 --> 02:12:32.576
Suddenly they have a true quality,
something imperative,


02:12:33.243 --> 02:12:35.495
almost beautiful.


02:12:41.835 --> 02:12:43.003
That was it.


02:12:44.462 --> 02:12:47.966
That was my... insight.


02:13:04.899 --> 02:13:08.069
You can go. I have nothing for you today.


02:13:11.281 --> 02:13:13.116
Kurt, would you come here for a minute?


02:13:32.010 --> 02:13:33.011
Yes?


02:13:33.345 --> 02:13:35.430
I'd like to see your art.


02:13:37.140 --> 02:13:38.224
When?


02:13:38.808 --> 02:13:42.312
Whenever you like, and if you like.


02:13:45.023 --> 02:13:46.566
Just let me know.


02:13:57.702 --> 02:13:59.454
What is there to think about?


02:14:01.164 --> 02:14:03.707
If he likes your art,
you'll get a gallery.


02:14:03.708 --> 02:14:06.378
- Then you can buy your girlfriend a car.
- I'm married.


02:14:07.087 --> 02:14:09.172
Then you can buy your wife
and your girlfriend a oar.


02:14:12.092 --> 02:14:14.969
I just don't know
if what I'm doing is good enough.


02:14:16.262 --> 02:14:17.847
Somehow it isn't.


02:14:19.766 --> 02:14:21.267
But it's all subjective anyway.


02:14:22.102 --> 02:14:24.145
And if it weren't subjective,
it'd be craft.


02:14:25.605 --> 02:14:27.565
It's also a matter of luck, you know?


02:14:28.775 --> 02:14:32.195
He's interested in your work,
for whatever reason. So you're in luck.


02:14:33.697 --> 02:14:38.992
He doesn't want to be wrong. He's ready
to see something brilliant in your work.


02:14:38.993 --> 02:14:40.370
Don't stand in your own way.


02:14:59.139 --> 02:15:01.141
It's good, your work. Really.


02:15:01.975 --> 02:15:03.101
It's good.


02:16:06.164 --> 02:16:09.209
During the war,
I was a Luftwaffe radio operator.


02:16:10.418 --> 02:16:13.379
I was a terrible radio operator,


02:16:14.172 --> 02:16:17.174
and my pilot was a terrible pilot.


02:16:17.175 --> 02:16:19.260
Well, we only had four weeks training.


02:16:20.512 --> 02:16:23.973
We were shot down
on our second sortie over the Crimea.


02:16:25.058 --> 02:16:26.893
The pilot was killed immediately.


02:16:44.369 --> 02:16:48.414
<i>Tatar nomads recovered me
from the wreckage</i>


02:16:49.374 --> 02:16:52.043
<i>with burns
that really should have killed me.</i>


02:16:54.712 --> 02:16:56.089
<i>These peasants,</i>


02:16:56.548 --> 02:17:00.176
the very same peasants I was supposed
to bomb, pulled me out of the wreckage...


02:17:01.845 --> 02:17:04.848
and looked after me as best they could.


02:17:07.141 --> 02:17:09.269
They rubbed grease into my wounds...


02:17:10.770 --> 02:17:12.730
and wrapped me in felt blankets.


02:17:22.073 --> 02:17:23.783
<i>I stayed with them for a year.</i>


02:17:24.158 --> 02:17:27.120
<i>Then I surrendered to the Americans
as a POW.</i>


02:17:44.596 --> 02:17:47.557
If I ask myself what I truly know,


02:17:48.349 --> 02:17:50.810
what I've truly experienced in life,


02:17:51.603 --> 02:17:54.772
what I can claim without lying...


02:17:57.025 --> 02:17:59.777
it's the grease on my skin.


02:18:00.612 --> 02:18:04.657
The home that is grease and felt.


02:18:06.451 --> 02:18:12.122
When other people tell me about love...
for their wives, for their children,


02:18:12.123 --> 02:18:15.460
or about sex, I know what they mean...


02:18:16.669 --> 02:18:20.548
only because I experienced
grease and felt on my skin.


02:18:27.055 --> 02:18:28.723
My life until then was uneventful.


02:18:30.016 --> 02:18:32.142
My childhood was happy and sheltered.


02:18:32.143 --> 02:18:34.228
A couple of slaps across the ears,
not many.


02:18:35.313 --> 02:18:36.856
My teachers liked me.


02:18:38.066 --> 02:18:40.068
I wanted to be a businessman, like my dad.


02:18:40.360 --> 02:18:42.236
I had no "artistic talent."


02:18:43.988 --> 02:18:47.574
And my life since was pretty uneventful.


02:18:47.575 --> 02:18:49.452
I'm still cheerful.


02:18:51.496 --> 02:18:53.122
I spent the last days of the war


02:18:53.790 --> 02:18:58.336
in an army hospital with friendly nurses,
very friendly nurses.


02:18:58.836 --> 02:19:02.924
Afterwards, fairly quick success
and this professorship here.


02:19:09.389 --> 02:19:10.515
But...


02:19:14.394 --> 02:19:16.771
the grease and the felt...


02:19:17.897 --> 02:19:22.276
those I absorbed
and understood so thoroughly...


02:19:23.319 --> 02:19:26.238
like Descartes understood that he existed.


02:19:26.239 --> 02:19:28.282
"I think, therefore I am."


02:19:31.035 --> 02:19:33.537
He questioned everything. Everything.


02:19:33.538 --> 02:19:37.290
Everything could be an illusion,
a trick, his imagination.


02:19:37.291 --> 02:19:40.503
But then he realized that something
was thinking those thoughts.


02:19:41.212 --> 02:19:43.631
So consequently, something must exist.


02:19:43.965 --> 02:19:45.841
And that something,


02:19:45.842 --> 02:19:47.969
he decided to call "myself."


02:19:51.347 --> 02:19:52.890
But who are you?


02:19:56.477 --> 02:19:57.979
What are you?


02:20:02.859 --> 02:20:03.901
This...


02:20:05.862 --> 02:20:07.030
This is not you.


02:22:19.162 --> 02:22:20.371
How was your day?


02:22:22.206 --> 02:22:23.541
Productive.


02:22:43.853 --> 02:22:45.188
Villa Cimbrone.


02:22:50.693 --> 02:22:53.654
- That's also Villa Cimbrone.
- No, Villa Rufolo.


02:22:53.988 --> 02:22:55.364
But also in Ravello.


02:23:00.411 --> 02:23:01.913
Such a beautiful car!


02:23:07.793 --> 02:23:09.003
Our hotel.


02:23:09.670 --> 02:23:11.005
Le Sirenuse.


02:23:17.595 --> 02:23:19.305
Oh God, Pompeii.


02:23:37.323 --> 02:23:39.283
Still a student at 30?


02:23:41.994 --> 02:23:44.997
When I was 30,
I was senior physician in Dresden.


02:23:45.915 --> 02:23:47.875
When Mozart was 30...


02:23:49.043 --> 02:23:50.336
he was dead.


02:23:54.632 --> 02:23:57.677
I understand you no longer want
my financial support.


02:23:57.927 --> 02:23:59.387
And I find that laudable.


02:24:00.596 --> 02:24:02.181
So I have a suggestion.


02:24:02.807 --> 02:24:05.976
I know the director
of the gynecology clinic in Dusseldorf.


02:24:05.977 --> 02:24:08.688
I'm frequently invited there
for consultations.


02:24:09.188 --> 02:24:13.024
I'll ask him
to give you a part-time job there.


02:24:13.025 --> 02:24:14.402
Something suitable.


02:24:15.653 --> 02:24:18.656
Maybe three hours each morning?


02:24:21.534 --> 02:24:23.327
Then you'll have an income,


02:24:24.078 --> 02:24:27.373
and you'll still have
ample time to... paint.


02:24:36.173 --> 02:24:38.342
Can't he just leave us alone?


02:24:40.553 --> 02:24:42.430
Can't he just vanish from our lives?


02:24:45.224 --> 02:24:47.810
Perhaps the job in the clinic
will help with that.


02:25:11.917 --> 02:25:14.712
DUSSELDORF GYNECOLOGY CLINIC


02:26:19.902 --> 02:26:22.112
White on a white background?


02:26:22.113 --> 02:26:23.280
Is this modern art?


02:26:26.283 --> 02:26:28.828
<i>Allegory of Emptiness.
That</i> could be <i>the title.</i>


02:26:29.620 --> 02:26:31.122
Maybe it will cause a sensation.


02:26:33.541 --> 02:26:37.294
Come on, I'll take you to dinner.
My driver's waiting outside.


02:27:07.450 --> 02:27:10.410
This has to be taken
to the passport office in Bonn


02:27:10.411 --> 02:27:12.955
so they can issue me a permanent document.


02:27:13.539 --> 02:27:16.792
It's ready to be picked up.
Here's your authorization.


02:27:17.960 --> 02:27:22.047
I was thinking, you live close to Bonn.
Why don't you do it for me?


02:27:22.423 --> 02:27:24.758
That way you can earn a bit more money.


02:27:25.301 --> 02:27:29.096
I'll come by next week
to pick up the passport. All right?


02:27:32.016 --> 02:27:34.560
- Can I bring you a coffee, Professor?
- Yes, thank you.


02:27:40.065 --> 02:27:41.817
Burghart Kroll arrested!


02:27:42.109 --> 02:27:45.361
Head of euthanasia program
lived undisturbed for ten years


02:27:45.362 --> 02:27:47.072
as consultant in Schleswig-Holstein.


02:27:50.075 --> 02:27:51.243
Ten cents.


02:27:52.578 --> 02:27:53.746
Thank you.


02:27:55.623 --> 02:27:56.749
Murderer of the sick.


02:28:01.337 --> 02:28:03.005
Murderer of the sick. Ten cents.


02:28:03.923 --> 02:28:06.382
- Thank you, sir. Good-bye.
- Ciao, my boy.


02:28:06.383 --> 02:28:08.385
- Professor, your coffee.
- Thanks.


02:28:34.245 --> 02:28:35.454
You smoke?


02:28:39.583 --> 02:28:42.378
Sixty-three is the right age to start.


02:28:43.420 --> 02:28:45.548
The consequences
will hardly catch up with me.


02:28:57.351 --> 02:28:59.895
You finish your meal.
I'm afraid I have to dash.


02:29:04.650 --> 02:29:05.859
Give my best to Ellie.


02:29:17.079 --> 02:29:19.415
- Good night.
- Good night, Professor.


02:30:14.470 --> 02:30:15.596
May I have a look?


02:30:16.096 --> 02:30:18.474
Keep it. I only need the sports pages.


02:30:18.724 --> 02:30:19.975
Thank you.


02:30:48.212 --> 02:30:49.588
"White On White."


02:30:50.839 --> 02:30:52.341
<i>Allegory of Emptiness.</i>


02:30:53.759 --> 02:30:55.094
Your father-in-law?


02:30:58.972 --> 02:31:00.182
What an asshole.


02:31:02.434 --> 02:31:04.060
You know, for the first time,


02:31:04.061 --> 02:31:06.063
I want success for another
more than for myself.


02:31:07.856 --> 02:31:10.943
Your mistake is clinging
to an easel and canvas.


02:31:12.069 --> 02:31:13.737
Painting is dead.


02:31:14.279 --> 02:31:19.493
Just like folk dancing
and lace-making and silent movies.


02:31:27.543 --> 02:31:30.504
I only want what's best for you,
or I'd just let you carry on.


02:31:33.424 --> 02:31:35.426
It's too late for us
to become doctors now.


02:31:57.114 --> 02:32:01.535
MURDERER OF THE SICK
ARRESTED AFTER 18 YEARS


02:32:30.898 --> 02:32:33.442
MURDERER OF THE SICK


02:40:49.896 --> 02:40:50.939
Kun?


02:41:13.169 --> 02:41:15.046
- Hello.
- Hello.


02:41:19.592 --> 02:41:20.844
What's this?


02:41:21.678 --> 02:41:23.805
I don't know either,
but I think that's it.


02:41:26.099 --> 02:41:27.517
Painted copies of photographs?


02:41:46.077 --> 02:41:47.162
Excuse me.


02:46:28.026 --> 02:46:30.652
Overall,
I am content with the construction.


02:46:30.653 --> 02:46:32.905
That's good to hear, Professor Seeband.


02:46:33.448 --> 02:46:35.783
- I've explained what concerns me.
- Yes.


02:46:39.704 --> 02:46:43.206
The clear door width
to the operating rooms must be


02:46:43.207 --> 02:46:45.043
augmented by 25 centimeters on both sides.


02:46:46.294 --> 02:46:49.588
That way, the larger beds
can still fit through comfortably.


02:46:49.589 --> 02:46:53.051
That's correct.
Thank you for your suggestion, Professor.


02:47:04.729 --> 02:47:07.815
I think you understand
why I didn't introduce you this morning.


02:47:08.316 --> 02:47:10.026
It wouldn't have been appropriate.


02:47:11.653 --> 02:47:14.822
How's the world of art? And,
more importantly, do you have my passport?


02:48:19.762 --> 02:48:20.930
<i>L.</i>


02:48:24.016 --> 02:48:26.436
Unfortunately, I have to go.


02:48:31.315 --> 02:48:32.608
Thanks.


02:48:35.361 --> 02:48:36.404
Excuse me.


02:48:58.009 --> 02:48:59.802
Have you ever seen anything like that?


02:49:01.262 --> 02:49:03.431
What did you say to him?
What's wrong with him?


02:51:13.644 --> 02:51:15.938
If you only knew
how beautiful you look right now.


02:51:17.940 --> 02:51:19.191
I'm pregnant.


02:51:21.736 --> 02:51:22.945
In the fourth month!


02:51:23.779 --> 02:51:26.324
I went to the doctor.
We're going to be parents!


02:51:27.825 --> 02:51:29.702
We're going to be parents after all!


02:52:01.150 --> 02:52:04.236
It's Sunday.
There's nobody here. I promise.


02:52:06.280 --> 02:52:08.282
Please, there's no one here.


02:52:09.951 --> 02:52:11.535
Please, like yesterday.


02:52:12.161 --> 02:52:15.331
Tell me again
and then come down the stairs.


02:52:27.259 --> 02:52:28.636
I'm pregnant.


02:53:13.597 --> 02:53:15.391
It's not potatoes, is it?


02:53:19.353 --> 02:53:21.814
How about I become your gallerist?


02:53:22.732 --> 02:53:24.942
Adrian Schimmel, the gallerist?


02:53:25.985 --> 02:53:27.028
Adrian Finck.


02:54:43.604 --> 02:54:45.022
We should begin.


02:54:48.609 --> 02:54:51.737
Are there any questions for Kurt Barnert?


02:54:55.658 --> 02:54:57.659
Then perhaps I will pose
the first question.


02:54:57.660 --> 02:54:59.244
Mr. Barnert,


02:54:59.245 --> 02:55:03.666
many of your paintings are based
on amateur photographs or magazines.


02:55:04.083 --> 02:55:08.337
<i>But the picture
Nude Descending</i> a <i>Staircase...</i>


02:55:09.463 --> 02:55:12.466
is surely a homage to Duchamp?


02:55:16.679 --> 02:55:17.847
Yes.


02:55:22.643 --> 02:55:24.562
<i>Heinz Viersen, Westdeutsche Zeitung.</i>


02:55:25.020 --> 02:55:28.731
Mr. Barnert, in your magnificent painting
Mother and Child,


02:55:28.732 --> 02:55:31.734
which we see here, who is depicted?


02:55:31.735 --> 02:55:33.028
You and your mother?


02:55:36.490 --> 02:55:39.118
No, it's just an amateur snapshot.


02:55:42.079 --> 02:55:44.039
It doesn't really matter to me
who I paint.


02:55:45.457 --> 02:55:48.752
But if you paint a portrait,
you must know the person.


02:55:49.587 --> 02:55:51.672
It's actually better if I don't know them.


02:55:53.048 --> 02:55:54.884
Then I see better what's really there.


02:55:57.678 --> 02:56:00.931
Is that the reason behind the passport
photos from a photo booth?


02:56:01.557 --> 02:56:03.392
A photograph without an author?


02:56:06.020 --> 02:56:07.062
Yes.


02:56:07.730 --> 02:56:09.814
So by painting a Wehrmacht officer,


02:56:09.815 --> 02:56:11.984
you aren't making a statement
about the Wehrmacht?


02:56:12.568 --> 02:56:16.447
No, I don't make statements.
I make pictures.


02:56:17.156 --> 02:56:19.992
Photographs... Photographs by other means.


02:56:20.910 --> 02:56:22.703
Hermann Schreiber, SDR.


02:56:23.495 --> 02:56:26.916
You take the exact composition
from a snapshot.


02:56:27.625 --> 02:56:29.627
Surely that means everything is random.


02:56:31.170 --> 02:56:32.755
Not random.


02:56:34.632 --> 02:56:37.009
Real. Coherent. Consistent.


02:56:38.719 --> 02:56:40.553
Only reality is consistent.


02:56:40.554 --> 02:56:42.556
Every reality is consistent.


02:56:44.725 --> 02:56:46.602
Everything that's true is beautiful.


02:56:47.603 --> 02:56:49.021
What do you mean by that?


02:56:55.361 --> 02:56:57.404
Let's suppose I say six numbers
to you now.


02:56:58.113 --> 02:57:00.616
It's just stupid. Pointless.


02:57:00.991 --> 02:57:05.913
But if the six numbers are the winning
lottery numbers, then they mean something.


02:57:06.330 --> 02:57:09.375
They have consistency,
value, almost beauty.


02:57:10.084 --> 02:57:12.002
It's the same with the photographs.


02:57:12.878 --> 02:57:14.296
I want the truth.


02:57:33.399 --> 02:57:34.900
Yes, Mr. Meybert?


02:57:35.651 --> 02:57:37.945
<i>Urs Meybert, Kunstchronik.</i>


02:57:38.779 --> 02:57:42.241
What will be next for you? More painted,
blurry copies of photographs?


02:57:43.325 --> 02:57:45.661
No, I've had enough of them for a while.


02:57:46.370 --> 02:57:48.664
I'm more interested in color charts now.


02:57:49.373 --> 02:57:50.624
Color charts?


02:57:51.166 --> 02:57:52.293
Yes.


02:57:56.547 --> 02:57:57.965
That'll get us into trouble.


02:58:02.303 --> 02:58:03.929
That'll get us into trouble too.


02:58:11.061 --> 02:58:15.231
Magazine images chosen at random,
photo booth passport photos,


02:58:15.232 --> 02:58:17.817
snapshots from family albums.


02:58:17.818 --> 02:58:20.112
All reproduced in painting, but blurred.


02:58:20.946 --> 02:58:25.701
With these pictures, which have
genuine force in some mysterious way,


02:58:26.118 --> 02:58:31.039
Kurt Barnert seems to be developing
into the leading artist of his generation.


02:58:31.040 --> 02:58:34.000
And that while working in a medium
that is often considered dead. Painting.


02:58:34.501 --> 02:58:35.627
But,


02:58:36.295 --> 02:58:40.758
like many of his generation,
he has no stories to tell, nothing to say.


02:58:41.091 --> 02:58:43.092
He parts with artistic tradition,


02:58:43.093 --> 02:58:46.512
breaks with
an autobiographical approach to art.


02:58:46.513 --> 02:58:49.974
So for the first time
in the history of art,


02:58:49.975 --> 02:58:52.478
we can speak of a work without an author.


02:58:53.771 --> 02:58:54.772
Was that good?


02:58:55.522 --> 02:58:56.523
Great.


02:59:09.203 --> 02:59:11.080
Sure I can't drive you to your hotel?


02:59:11.872 --> 02:59:13.540
I'd like to walk a bit.


02:59:16.126 --> 02:59:17.461
You were good today.


02:59:18.295 --> 02:59:19.338
It was good.


02:59:20.839 --> 02:59:21.924
It's going to be good.

